window.TOTK_VM_DATA = [{"seq":1,"id":"vm_rauru_001","no":"No.001","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1690,"y":379,"z":2334,"gx":379,"gy":-1690,"gz":2334,"title_zh":"左纳乌神木","title_en":"Sacred Tree of the Zonai","place_zh":"初始空岛","place_en":"Great Sky Island","transcript_zh":"这株神木随我们部族欣欣向荣、繁衍生息……听说曾有一段时间是在这里举办祭祀活动的。即便如今祭祀的场所已经转移到了时之神殿，我想神木也一定还在守望着我们。","transcript_en":"The lives of our people and this tree are interconnected. As we prospered, so too did it. It was the site for many of our rituals, and though that role has since been taken up by the Temple of Time, I am sure this sacred tree watches over us still."},{"seq":2,"id":"vm_rauru_002","no":"No.002","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":165,"y":365,"z":2298,"gx":365,"gy":-165,"gz":2298,"title_zh":"逐渐消失的遗产","title_en":"Fading Legacy","place_zh":"觉醒室","place_en":"Room of Awakening","transcript_zh":"电池制造机。因为制造过程复杂，只有极少数的魔像能胜任，如今还在运作的制造点仅剩两处，但对于现在来说也足够了。据说以前王国内到处都能见到……","transcript_en":"A crystal refinery, and one responsible for a highly complex manufacturing process. The nature of the work was such that only a select few constructs could perform it, and only two of those remain in operation. Fortunately that is enough for now, though apparently there was a time when they could be found throughout the kingdom..."},{"seq":3,"id":"vm_rauru_003","no":"No.003","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":899,"y":452,"z":1446,"gx":452,"gy":-899,"gz":1446,"title_zh":"驱邪破魔之楔","title_en":"Piercing Evil","place_zh":"时之神殿","place_en":"Temple of Time","transcript_zh":"时之神殿是举办王国祭祀活动的场所，也是报时的钟楼。其朝天部分外伸延展，朝地部分内缩尖锐的形状，便是传统的左纳乌建筑风格，据说古时候这种形状还兼具驱邪破魔之楔的作用。","transcript_en":"The Temple of Time is a bell tower and faithful time keeper as well as a spiritual center of this land. It was constructed in a traditional Zonai architectural style that extends both up into the sky and down into the ground. It was believed in ancient times that such a design could pierce through evil."},{"seq":4,"id":"vm_rauru_004","no":"No.004","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":638,"y":453,"z":1472,"gx":453,"gy":-638,"gz":1472,"title_zh":"祭坛","title_en":"The Altar","place_zh":"时之神殿","place_en":"Temple of Time","transcript_zh":"这里是向上天献上贡品，祈求太平盛世和丰饶的祭坛，被视为神殿之中最神圣的地方。自古就流传着和神圣之力产生反应便能穿越时空的传说，这座祭坛或许拥有着连我都从未听闻过的功能","transcript_en":"This altar is considered the most holy place in the temple, and it is where we give offerings as part of our prayers for a bountiful, peaceful world. I have heard ancient legends that it could interact with a sacred power, allowing travel back and forth through time... Though how this was done is a mystery to me."},{"seq":5,"id":"vm_rauru_005","no":"No.005","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1032,"y":403,"z":1422,"gx":403,"gy":-1032,"gz":1422,"title_zh":"森林鸵鸟","title_en":"The Forest Ostrich","place_zh":"时之庭院","place_en":"Garden of Time","transcript_zh":"根据王后的提议，我们决定保护濒临灭绝的森林驼鸟。它们原本生活在寒冷地带但似乎有着很强的环境适应能力，如今它们的数量增长了许多，除了极地地带，已经随处可见了。","transcript_en":"The forest ostriches were once on the brink of extinction. However, a proposal by the queen was made to protect them, and eventually this species flourished once more. Though they were originally only found in colder lands, they are highly adaptable, thriving in all but the frigid polar regions."},{"seq":6,"id":"vm_rauru_006","no":"No.006","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":946,"y":323,"z":1442,"gx":323,"gy":-946,"gz":1442,"title_zh":"能源运输线","title_en":"Energy Lines","place_zh":"时之庭院","place_en":"Garden of Time","transcript_zh":"这是用来搬运材料的轨道，同时具备通过管线运输能源的作用。在鼓隆族的村庄也能经常看到像这样使用轨道的设施，但要追本溯源的话，他们应该是模仿了我们提供的技术","transcript_en":"These rails are intended to transport materials, but they also supply energy through pipes. The Goron people make extensive use of this kind of mechanism, and I believe it is possible they modeled their designs on our own technology..."},{"seq":7,"id":"vm_rauru_007","no":"No.007","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1083,"y":176,"z":1415,"gx":176,"gy":-1083,"gz":1415,"title_zh":"魔像的秩序","title_en":"Construct Compassion","place_zh":"时之庭院","place_en":"Garden of Time","transcript_zh":"我见过魔像按照顺序排成一列的情景。似乎是因为能源供给处太少而造成了拥堵，但除了它们会整齐排队等待，我还发现它们会让能源较少的魔像优先进行补给。如果人也能维持这样的秩序","transcript_en":"On occasion, constructs have been observed forming a line as they wait for an available charging spot. More interestingly, some will give up their place in that line to allow constructs with a greater need to recharge first. Were it that everyone always acted with such empathy..."},{"seq":8,"id":"vm_rauru_008","no":"No.008","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1169,"y":115,"z":1417,"gx":115,"gy":-1169,"gz":1417,"title_zh":"模仿试吃","title_en":"A Sense of Taste","place_zh":"时之庭院","place_en":"Garden of Time","transcript_zh":"我们不仅让料理魔像学会了烹饪料理，还给它们灌输了药物知识。它们没有感知味觉的器官，但通过模仿我们渐渐学会了试吃的动作，给魔像们赋予学习能力的姐姐本人都大吃了一惊。","transcript_en":"Our Culinary Constructs were imparted with knowledge of both cooking meals and concocting medicines. Though they have no taste buds, they learned to mimic the movements we make when tasting food. Even my sister, who gifted them with the ability to learn in the first place, was surprised by what they glean through simple observation."},{"seq":9,"id":"vm_rauru_009","no":"No.009","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1675,"y":446,"z":1442,"gx":446,"gy":-1675,"gz":1442,"title_zh":"不断思考","title_en":"Musings","place_zh":"时之庭院","place_en":"Garden of Time","transcript_zh":"这些东西被称为左纳乌装置制造机，全凭运气的想法在我们的文明中极其少见，我认为它一定另有用途。我猜测这东西单纯只是用来娱乐的……可能设计者并不是左纳乌族……祖先们的想法有时难以理解，但像这样思考各种可能也挺有趣的。","transcript_en":"This is known as a Zonai device dispenser, but the concept of leaving things to chance is not one often seen in our civilization. I myself believe that it was originally created with a different purpose. Maybe it was used for entertainment, or maybe it was not even originally made by the Zonai... The ways of our ancestors are sometimes unclear, but they are also interesting puzzles to unravel."},{"seq":10,"id":"vm_rauru_010","no":"No.010","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1517,"y":492,"z":1439,"gx":492,"gy":-1517,"gz":1439,"title_zh":"空岛的守卫","title_en":"Sky Island Guardians","place_zh":"初始空岛","place_en":"Great Sky Island","transcript_zh":"控制方块魔像只在战斗时变形，大幅削减了待机时的能源消耗，但目前魔像只能在能源供给点上运行，这仍然是我们难以解决的问题。姐姐想对魔像进行改良，让它可以持续追踪敌人直至天涯海角……可她也在抱怨古人制作的设计图太难解读。","transcript_en":"Though the Flux Constructs can enter a standby mode, reducing energy consumption outside of battle, they remain one of our less energy-efficient creations. Considering their limitations, I would love to improve on their design and give them greater range, but my sister says the ancients' schematics for them are quite abstruse."},{"seq":11,"id":"vm_rauru_011","no":"No.011","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1626,"y":634,"z":1485,"gx":634,"gy":-1626,"gz":1485,"title_zh":"人工创造的银色世界","title_en":"Crafted Snowscape","place_zh":"初始空岛","place_en":"Great Sky Island","transcript_zh":"为了测试魔像和左纳乌装置的耐久性，我们搭建了这片地方。我们利用冰龙头的技术让冷气在整座岛上循环，然后成功创造出了这片能永远存续的银色世界。索尼娅第一次来到这里时，惊得瞪大了双眼。","transcript_en":"It was here that we used the capabilities of frost emitters to create a permanently snowy region. By encircling the island in cold air, we created an ideal place to test the durability of constructs and Zonai devices. I'll always remember the look of wonder on Sonia's face the first time we came here."},{"seq":12,"id":"vm_rauru_012","no":"No.012","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1287,"y":742,"z":1562,"gx":742,"gy":-1287,"gz":1562,"title_zh":"禁止双人搭乘","title_en":"Solo Riders Only","place_zh":"初始空岛","place_en":"Great Sky Island","transcript_zh":"飞行场原本是在空岛之间移动或搬运物资的一种手段。我们曾设想让海拉鲁的人们也能使用它，但操作起来很是困难，所以未能得到普及。索尼娅练习飞行时，我也想跟着搭乘，结果却被魔像阻止了，对我说禁止双人搭乘","transcript_en":"We intended for this airfield to allow easy transportation of goods between sky islands—while I hoped the people of Hyrule would make use of it, the flying machines proved challenging to control. I once sought to join Sonia while she practiced with one, but a construct stopped me, insisting that the devices are limited to one rider..."},{"seq":13,"id":"vm_rauru_013","no":"No.013","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1357,"y":634,"z":1427,"gx":634,"gy":-1357,"gz":1427,"title_zh":"新人魔像","title_en":"Inexperienced Constructs","place_zh":"初始空岛","place_en":"Great Sky Island","transcript_zh":"木匠魔像。没有人比它们更懂得如何使用左纳乌装置了吧。但正因为它们拥有学习能力，所以就需要特别留意新人魔像的状况。曾经因为风扇机方向设置得不对，导致木筏朝着错误的方向前进，费了好大劲才返回了原处……索尼娅倒是乐在其中，我却吓出一身冷汗。","transcript_en":"I do not believe anyone else is as proficient at handling Zonai devices as the Maker Constructs. That said, one should be careful around the inventions of less experienced ones. I recall a very chaotic rafting ride when a misaligned fan made it nearly impossible to steer. I was scared half to death throughout, but Queen Sonia enjoyed herself."},{"seq":14,"id":"vm_rauru_014","no":"No.014","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1005,"y":1847,"z":861,"gx":1847,"gy":-1005,"gz":861,"title_zh":"圆环","title_en":"Circular Design","place_zh":"北哈特尔天空诸岛","place_en":"North Necluda Sky Archipelago","transcript_zh":"圆环的设计有着缘分长久和驱魔辟邪的意义。在这座岛上也能看见许多圆环状的建筑，多是用来保存重要记录的书库，但现在只留存着由姐姐负责管理的东西。","transcript_en":"Circular designs often represent an eternal bond and were even thought to ward off evil. Perhaps with that in mind, many of the structures here have been constructed with a circular shape. Though this was once an archive containing many important records, now only those my sister keeps remain."},{"seq":15,"id":"vm_rauru_015","no":"No.015","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":1702,"y":2396,"z":1475,"gx":2396,"gy":-1702,"gz":1475,"title_zh":"左纳尼乌姆制炼之岛","title_en":"Zonaite Forge Island","place_zh":"左纳尼乌姆制炼之岛","place_en":"Zonaite Forge Island","transcript_zh":"空岛曾经也盛产左纳尼乌姆，但任谁都未曾料想过未来某天资源会枯竭殆尽……这座巨大的精炼场就是那时候留下的。这里还留有作为动力源的熔岩，找姐姐商量一下这个炉子能不能在其他地方派上用场","transcript_en":"Zonaite was once readily found even on sky islands; this giant refinery is a remnant of a time where its scarcity seemed impossible. Of course, the lava that powered the refinery still remains. I should consult with my sister and see whether we can yet find a use for this furnace..."},{"seq":16,"id":"vm_rauru_016","no":"No.016","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":864,"y":4448,"z":2620,"gx":4448,"gy":-864,"gz":2620,"title_zh":"测试大勇之岛","title_en":"Valor Island","place_zh":"测试大勇之岛","place_en":"Valor Island","transcript_zh":"完成勇跃仪式的人将获得强化自身的装束。装束可以让你在空中更容易控制身体，集齐并穿上所有装束后，无论从多高的地方坠落，都可以化解掉冲击力。古代左纳乌人坠落到地上却没有受到致命伤，靠的就是这套装束吧。","transcript_en":"Those that complete the skydiving trial are bestowed empowering attire. It allows them to better control their movement in the air, and if all the pieces are worn together, the wearer need not fear striking the ground no matter how far they fall. The ancient Zonai even fell to the surface at times, but I believe this attire kept them safe too."},{"seq":17,"id":"vm_rauru_017","no":"No.017","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-293,"y":3644,"z":1192,"gx":3644,"gy":293,"gz":1192,"title_zh":"低重力空间","title_en":"Low-Gravity Space","place_zh":"水涌之岛","place_en":"Wellspring Island","transcript_zh":"听说这片可以操控重力的空间原本是为了缓冲搬运物品时的冲击力而被开发出来的。即便在空中也能像在水中一样行动，这让卓拉族很是开心。","transcript_en":"I have heard that the original reason for the lower gravity in this space was to reduce the jolts cargo could experience during transit. However, it has an additional use; it seems the Zora greatly enjoy the sensation of swimming through the sky."},{"seq":18,"id":"vm_rauru_018","no":"No.018","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-406,"y":3578,"z":1202,"gx":3578,"gy":406,"gz":1202,"title_zh":"浮游水球","title_en":"Floating Spheres of Water","place_zh":"水涌之岛","place_en":"Wellspring Island","transcript_zh":"我们在这里利用丰富的水源开展了各种关于水的研究。浮游水球被誉为是能够改变世界物流的发明，但因为无法长时间维持形状，它的应用还仅限于一部分岛屿。","transcript_en":"Thanks to the plentiful water available here, this is a prime spot for conducting water-related research. The floating spheres, for example, have the potential to revolutionize logistics, but as they do not retain their shape for long, their use is limited to certain islands."},{"seq":19,"id":"vm_rauru_019","no":"No.019","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-793,"y":3349,"z":1750,"gx":3349,"gy":793,"gz":1750,"title_zh":"水涌之岛","title_en":"Wellspring Island","place_zh":"水之神殿","place_en":"Water Temple","transcript_zh":"这片大水源会化作雨云和雨水滋润大地。自古就和左纳乌族有交流的卓拉族就是通过流向地面的巨大瀑布来到空中的吧。就是这瀑布将两族的关系连结在了一起。","transcript_en":"The water that flows from here eventually becomes clouds and rain, bringing water down to the land. The Zora people in ancient times had dealings with the Zonai, and I can imagine they used the immense waterfall to travel from the surface to the sky. Hmm. It is appropriate some refer to this waterfall as a bridge."},{"seq":20,"id":"vm_rauru_020","no":"No.020","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-538,"y":4080,"z":602,"gx":4080,"gy":538,"gz":602,"title_zh":"鱼鳞飞舞之岛","title_en":"Floating Scales Island","place_zh":"鱼鳞飞舞之岛","place_en":"Floating Scales Island","transcript_zh":"我听卓拉族说天空中有鱼时，还觉得他们这话说得也太奇怪了，但没想到居然是真的，令我大吃一惊。他们告诉我要站在鱼背中央往西南方眺望……原来如此……这种独特的思维很有卓拉族的风格。","transcript_en":"I thought it very strange when I heard from the Zora that there was a fish in the sky, but now I see what they meant. They also told me to stand on the edge of the center platform and look out to the southwest, but I... Oh... I understand! Mmm. Quite befitting the Zora."},{"seq":21,"id":"vm_rauru_021","no":"No.021","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-1505,"y":3702,"z":1162,"gx":3702,"gy":1505,"gz":1162,"title_zh":"投射装置","title_en":"Launch Mechanism","place_zh":"南阿卡莱天空诸岛","place_en":"Sokkala Sky Archipelago","transcript_zh":"能看到许多坠落至地上的东西。恐怕是曾在这里周转的货物吧……原来如此……也许是因为容器的形状特殊，投射失败导致的结果。","transcript_en":"A lot of debris is scattered in the area. It is likely that cargo was handled here and...hmm... Perhaps the strange shape of the container made it difficult to control the launch mechanism..."},{"seq":22,"id":"vm_rauru_022","no":"No.022","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-2128,"y":4525,"z":1160,"gx":4525,"gy":2128,"gz":1160,"title_zh":"采石之岛","title_en":"Sky Mine","place_zh":"采石之岛","place_en":"Sky Mine","transcript_zh":"这里漂浮着无数矿山，是矿石的产地，据说许多人为了追求财富来到这座岛……如今矿山已经所剩无几……但是两人静静眺望夜空中闪耀的矿床，这种感觉似乎也不赖。","transcript_en":"This area was once known for the abundance of ore that could be mined from the numerous floating islands. Many gathered here to make their fortunes, though today, only a few mines remain. The sight of ore deposits sparkling in the night sky—wonderful company at one's side—is a better kind of fortune, in any case..."},{"seq":23,"id":"vm_rauru_023","no":"No.023","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-3513,"y":4654,"z":1010,"gx":4654,"gy":3513,"gz":1010,"title_zh":"龙所司掌的迷宫","title_en":"Ruled by the Dragon","place_zh":"洛美岛上层","place_en":"Lomei Sky Labyrinth","transcript_zh":"这里也许曾是审判欺骗自我之人的地方。守护者之龙会将其灵魂置于勇气的天平上进行审视。据说在得到守护者的指引前，灵魂将永远在迷宫中徘徊……","transcript_en":"It is said that until the guardian of this labyrinth offered guidance, a soul would be set to wander these halls. Perhaps this was the room where those dishonest with themselves were judged...where the guardian of this place weighed the courage of a soul."},{"seq":24,"id":"vm_rauru_024","no":"No.024","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-2055,"y":221,"z":1988,"gx":221,"gy":2055,"gz":1988,"title_zh":"测试刚勇之岛","title_en":"Bravery Island","place_zh":"测试刚勇之岛","place_en":"Bravery Island","transcript_zh":"仅凭一副身躯翔空中，来掌握克服恐惧的本领，放在左纳乌装置普及的当下，已被视作陈旧的思想而遭到了淘汰。但如今只剩姐姐和我两个人了，我发自内心地感受到……正因为眼下的世界是这副状况，靠自己的力量去开辟道路有多么重要。","transcript_en":"In a time when Zonai devices make it easy to overcome many of life's obstacles, the idea of flying through the sky without assistance—of overcoming one's fear of falling—has been dismissed as unnecessary idealism. But now that only my sister and I remain, I believe, with my whole being, that it is more important than ever to always strive to grow."},{"seq":25,"id":"vm_rauru_025","no":"No.025","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-3535,"y":-955,"z":1011,"gx":-955,"gy":3535,"gz":1011,"title_zh":"枭所司掌的迷宫","title_en":"Ruled by the Owl","place_zh":"北洛美城堡上层","place_en":"North Lomei Castle Top Floor","transcript_zh":"这里也许曾是审判算计他者之人的地方。是虚构还是真实……智慧的守护者会凭借犀利的目光裁定是非善恶……据说在得到守护者的指引前，灵魂将永远在迷宫中律徊……","transcript_en":"I have heard that, until a soul here receives guidance from the labyrinth's guardian, it will wander this maze. Perhaps it was here, then, that the guardian of wisdom, with their keen mind, would pass judgment on those who deceived others..."},{"seq":26,"id":"vm_rauru_026","no":"No.026","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-2985,"y":-2813,"z":861,"gx":-2813,"gy":2985,"gz":861,"title_zh":"渡船","title_en":"Traversal Challenges","place_zh":"通往天空的连绵岛屿","place_en":"Rising Island Chain","transcript_zh":"虽然已经做好准备驱散前方的邪气了，但索尼娅也在……那么，要在这片天空移动就有点难了……这艘船还能启动吗……如果它还留有姐姐的魂之力，又或者……","transcript_en":"I traveled here on a quest to cleanse evil, and Sonia has accompanied me. However, I had not considered how challenging it would be to traverse this path. If I had my sister's power, I could perhaps move this vessel..."},{"seq":27,"id":"vm_rauru_027","no":"No.027","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-2927,"y":-2858,"z":1517,"gx":-2858,"gy":2927,"gz":1517,"title_zh":"天鸟船","title_en":"Stormwind Ark","place_zh":"风之神殿","place_en":"Wind Temple","transcript_zh":"“不慎跌落的左纳乌人，被利特的羽翼救起，感恩相赠天鸟船，羽翼悦然舞空起”……这是我们一族的古老传说，这艘船难道就是","transcript_en":"Ah, I think I remember...\n\"When a Zonai tumbled,\nRito wings gave chase.\nIn thanks for their salvation,\nThe Stormwind Ark was made.\nA gift given from the Zonai,\nAnd the Rito filled with joy.\"\nIt is an old legend of my people. Could this be that vessel?"},{"seq":28,"id":"vm_rauru_028","no":"No.028","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-927,"y":-2222,"z":1642,"gx":-2222,"gy":927,"gz":1642,"title_zh":"测试勇气之岛","title_en":"Courage Island","place_zh":"测试勇气之岛","place_en":"Courage Island","transcript_zh":"这座岛上举行的仪式要求挑战者精神、技巧、体能兼备才可通过。据说过去每个成年人都会参加这项考验，但自从左纳乌装置普及后，只有想测试自身勇气的挑战者才会来到此地……或许今后再也不会出现新的挑战者了吧","transcript_en":"The ceremony held here was a trial of heart, strength, and technique. There was a time where everyone who came of age would undertake this test, but as Zonai devices developed and spread, only those wishing to challenge their courage would take part. I wonder if this island will ever see a new challenger..."},{"seq":29,"id":"vm_rauru_029","no":"No.029","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":-1058,"y":-3680,"z":1796,"gx":-3680,"gy":1058,"gz":1796,"title_zh":"祓暗之岛","title_en":"Lightcast Island","place_zh":"祓暗之岛","place_en":"Lightcast Island","transcript_zh":"拥有光之力量的人会来到这座岛进行修炼。仅靠自己的光芒驱散潜伏于黑暗之中的邪恶……日复一日的修炼终将令其收获强大的破魔力量。我已记不清年幼时来此修炼过多少次了","transcript_en":"This island is a training site for those who carry the power of light. By practicing at length with this power, one can grow strong enough to overcome great evil. Oh, to recall all the times I had visited this place in my youth..."},{"seq":30,"id":"vm_rauru_030","no":"No.030","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":320,"y":-3493,"z":1931,"gx":-3493,"gy":-320,"gz":1931,"title_zh":"星见之岛","title_en":"Starview Island","place_zh":"星见之岛","place_en":"Starview Island","transcript_zh":"这些东西原本都是用来储存东西的，但很久以前就不再使用了。也不知是从何时起，这里有了星见之岛的名字。不过，此刻在我身旁双眼闪闪发光的索尼娅，才是属于我的星星","transcript_en":"Though this island was originally used as a place to store things, it has been a long time since it fulfilled that role. And while the island lacks an official name, many have come to call it Starview Island. As for me, the only real stars are those sparkling in Sonia's eyes..."},{"seq":31,"id":"vm_rauru_031","no":"No.031","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":2113,"y":-1722,"z":1149,"gx":-1722,"gy":-2113,"gz":1149,"title_zh":"逐渐崩塌的要塞","title_en":"Crumbling Fortress","place_zh":"东格鲁德天空诸岛","place_en":"East Gerudo Sky Archipelago","transcript_zh":"这岛是一座环绕着坚固壁垒的要塞，但崩塌的情况比其他岛更严重……是因为格鲁德地区干燥的气候吧……如果坠落到地面会酿成惨剧，必须尽早派遣木匠魔像修理","transcript_en":"This island was intended to be a fortress with a strong wall, but it seems to be collapsing faster than other islands... I wonder if the dry climate of the Gerudo region is at fault. Regardless, I should commission a Maker Construct to help as soon as possible; it would be a disaster if the island fell to the surface."},{"seq":32,"id":"vm_rauru_032","no":"No.032","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":3305,"y":-1794,"z":1010,"gx":-1794,"gy":-3305,"gz":1010,"title_zh":"野猪所司掌的迷宫","title_en":"Ruled by the Boar","place_zh":"南洛美城堡上层","place_en":"South Lomei Castle Top Floor","transcript_zh":"这里也许曾是审判卖弄力量之人的地方。也有传闻称此地过去上至于天，下至于渊，无比广阔。听闻受审之人须在力量守护者的监督下，摒弃傲慢的心境才能走出迷宫……","transcript_en":"There are stories that claim a soul will wander these halls until the guardian of power—said to reach from depths to sky, it was so large—has cleansed them of their pride. Perhaps it was in this room that judgment was passed on those overly boastful of their power..."},{"seq":33,"id":"vm_rauru_033","no":"No.033","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":2630,"y":721,"z":737,"gx":721,"gy":-2630,"gz":737,"title_zh":"雷鸣之岛","title_en":"Thunderhead Isles","place_zh":"雷鸣之岛","place_en":"Thunderhead Isles","transcript_zh":"这原来是汇集地底物资的空中港口，但如今由姐姐管理，用来保管魔像。戒备变得异常森严，就连我来这也要费不少工夫……既然是姐姐的安排……那一定有她的理由吧。","transcript_en":"This was originally a port where materials from the Depths were imported and stored, but it is currently being managed by my sister as a construct warehouse. Security is unusually tight—even I had trouble coming here—but knowing my sister, she has her reasons."},{"seq":34,"id":"vm_rauru_034","no":"No.034","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":2902,"y":895,"z":758,"gx":895,"gy":-2902,"gz":758,"title_zh":"雷龙信仰","title_en":"Faith in the Lightning Dragon","place_zh":"雷鸣之岛","place_en":"Thunderhead Isles","transcript_zh":"左纳乌族曾因落雷而烦恼，这便是原本用来解决问题而制造的避雷针，但地上百姓认为这是雷龙的加护，于是便发展成了对雷龙的信仰。所谓的信仰，或许就是偶然与必然交错之时的产物吧。","transcript_en":"The people on the surface believe this to be proof of the lightning dragon's divine protection. In actuality, it is a lightning rod the Zonai constructed to prevent lightning strikes. Perhaps this is how belief in the lightning dragon began... I wonder how often belief results from unrelated coincidence."},{"seq":35,"id":"vm_rauru_035","no":"No.035","narrator":"rauru","layer":20,"x":3111,"y":957,"z":755,"gx":957,"gy":-3111,"gz":755,"title_zh":"宝藏地图","title_en":"Treasure Maps","place_zh":"雷鸣之岛","place_en":"Thunderhead Isles","transcript_zh":"发现了一处叫人怀念的地方。幼时贪玩的我热衷于寻搜宝藏地图，不知不觉间，我已经熟知空岛的地形和左纳乌装置的使用方法。或许促使人学习任何事物的最好动力就是好奇心吧。","transcript_en":"I get a strong sense of nostalgia in this place. When I was young, I was intensely interested in finding and studying treasure maps. Before I knew it, I had become quite familiar with the topography of the sky islands and, incidentally, with Zonai devices. Hahaha...nothing motivates one to learn like a healthy sense of curiosity."},{"seq":36,"id":"vm_zelda_001","no":"No.001","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-613,"y":-253,"z":42,"gx":-253,"gy":613,"gz":42,"title_zh":"海拉鲁城堡大门","title_en":"Hyrule Castle Gates","place_zh":"海拉鲁城堡大门","place_en":"Hyrule Castle Gate","transcript_zh":"城堡大门。父王曾拍着胸脯保证这里绝不可能被摧毁，实际上也确实只有这扇大门毫发无伤。据说是希卡族智慧与鼓隆族技术融合而成的结晶。","transcript_en":"I have heard the castle gate is the product of Sheikah wisdom and Goron engineering. Father always said it would never fall, and he was technically correct; it is the only part of the castle that remains unblemished."},{"seq":37,"id":"vm_zelda_002","no":"No.002","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-871,"y":-102,"z":104,"gx":-102,"gy":871,"gz":104,"title_zh":"王族餐桌","title_en":"The Royal Family's Dining Table","place_zh":"餐厅","place_en":"Dining Room","transcript_zh":"食堂。父王生前很喜欢壁炉前面的座位。我还记得林克总是站在门口等到我吃完……有一次我吃了足足3个水果蛋糕他的脸上写满了惊讶，现在想起来还是很好笑。","transcript_en":"The dining hall... Father was partial to the seat in front of the fireplace, and Link preferred to stand watch near the entrance while I ate. I still laugh when I remember the look of surprise on Link's face as I returned for my second...and then third helping of fruit cake."},{"seq":38,"id":"vm_zelda_003","no":"No.003","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-746,"y":-254,"z":104,"gx":-254,"gy":746,"gz":104,"title_zh":"一去不返的景色","title_en":"A Missing View","place_zh":"观察室","place_en":"Observation Room","transcript_zh":"观察室。以前我很喜欢从这里眺望城邑。可现在映入眼帘的景色已经截然不同……我一定会让从前的美景恢复如初。","transcript_en":"I loved gazing out at castle town here in the observation room... The view is completely different now, but...I will see to its restoration."},{"seq":39,"id":"vm_zelda_004","no":"No.004","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-830,"y":-356,"z":109,"gx":-356,"gy":830,"gz":109,"title_zh":"坚不可摧的城寨","title_en":"Sturdy Fortifications","place_zh":"三殿","place_en":"First Gatehouse","transcript_zh":"三殿。海拉鲁城堡抵御进攻的最外侧防线。城墙上有不少崩塌的地方，但塔楼的部分似乎受损较轻。这里看起来比较适合作为重建城堡的出发点，回头就让他们把这里设为建材放置场吧。","transcript_en":"The first gatehouse is the outermost point of entry to Hyrule Castle. While the ramparts themselves are crumbling in many places, the towers appear to have endured. This seems like an excellent place to store the materials we will need as we work to restore the castle."},{"seq":40,"id":"vm_zelda_005","no":"No.005","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-829,"y":-356,"z":60,"gx":-356,"gy":829,"gz":60,"title_zh":"来龙去脉","title_en":"The Honest Truth","place_zh":"警卫室","place_en":"Guards' Chamber","transcript_zh":"训练所。没有护卫任务的时候，林克也经常在这里和其他士兵挥洒汗水。我还记得有一次，我尝试射箭却脱了靶，结果箭刚好穿过火把点燃了别的地方，最后大家一起慌慌张张地把火灭掉了","transcript_en":"The guards' chamber. When he was not occupied by his duties as my protector, Link would often come here to train alongside the regular soldiers. Hm... They once let me join in, but the arrow I loosed went...off target. It also caught the flame of a torch, and everyone frantically raced to put out the resulting fire..."},{"seq":41,"id":"vm_zelda_006","no":"No.006","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1110,"y":-400,"z":22,"gx":-400,"gy":1110,"gz":22,"title_zh":"传说中的大盗","title_en":"The Great Bandit","place_zh":"牢房","place_en":"Lockup","transcript_zh":"牢房。据我所知，当时并没有罪行严重到要关进这里的犯人。最后一次入狱记录，是很久很久以前被逮捕归案的大盗—拉姆达……时至今日，他好像已经成了那些追求时尚之人口中的传说人物……","transcript_en":"As far as I am aware, there were never criminals foul enough to warrant imprisonment here. And while I do recall a bandit named \"Misko\" being captured long, long ago, it seems in recent times they have risen to greater fame for their keen sense of fashion."},{"seq":42,"id":"vm_zelda_007","no":"No.007","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1188,"y":-242,"z":10,"gx":-242,"gy":1188,"gz":10,"title_zh":"往日的繁华","title_en":"Busy Days Gone By","place_zh":"船坞","place_en":"Docks","transcript_zh":"船坞。以前这里的船只每天都络绎不绝。放眼商贩云集的城堡，这里是最热闹的地方。越是了解当时的景象有多么繁华，就越让人觉得如今荒无人烟的船坞有多么凄凉……","transcript_en":"Ships would come and go all day here at the docks. It truly was the most lively part of the castle, and it always felt thus thanks to the numerous merchants. It feels lonely now, abandoned as it is... A feeling magnified as I reflect on what it once was."},{"seq":43,"id":"vm_zelda_008","no":"No.008","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1069,"y":-156,"z":214,"gx":-156,"gy":1069,"gz":214,"title_zh":"秘密","title_en":"A King's Secret","place_zh":"图书馆","place_en":"Library","transcript_zh":"图书馆。现在虽然布满了灰尘，但大部分书籍打扫一下都还可以阅读。父王不喜欢读书，却会经常到这里来，不知道他都在做些什么……","transcript_en":"The castle's library, now covered in dust. At first glance, I found this worrying, but I believe nearly all the books can be salvaged with some effort. Though Father never cared much for books, he would often visit this place. I wonder why..."},{"seq":44,"id":"vm_zelda_009","no":"No.009","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1063,"y":-253,"z":335,"gx":-253,"gy":1063,"gz":335,"title_zh":"避难壕","title_en":"A Place of Shelter","place_zh":"王座厅","place_en":"Throne Room","transcript_zh":"渴见室。无主的王座默默叙述着一切王座背后的雕刻采用了十分坚固的构造，紧急情况下可以用来藏身，但听说从未被使用过。","transcript_en":"Though this throne sits vacant, the space it occupies still speaks volumes. For instance, while the sculpture behind the throne is especially sturdy and serves as a hiding place in an emergency, no one that occupied that seat has ever chosen to use it."},{"seq":45,"id":"vm_zelda_010","no":"No.010","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1066,"y":-255,"z":465,"gx":-255,"gy":1066,"gz":465,"title_zh":"不报时的钟","title_en":"The Bell That Tolled","place_zh":"钟楼","place_en":"Bell Tower","transcript_zh":"钟楼。为修行焦头烂额的那段时间，每当我听到这口钟敲响报时，就会深感自己的无力。而我……最后一次听到钟声……就是灾厄复活那天的警钟……","transcript_en":"The bell tower... My memories of it are filled with a terrible sense of helplessness. When that bell tolled, it reminded me that my training was incomplete. And the last time I heard it ring out, it was warning us of the Calamity's arrival."},{"seq":46,"id":"vm_zelda_011","no":"No.011","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-993,"y":-325,"z":300,"gx":-325,"gy":993,"gz":300,"title_zh":"冰冷的床铺","title_en":"A Neglected Room","place_zh":"塞尔达公主的房间","place_en":"Princess Zelda's Room","transcript_zh":"我的房间。不过晚上我大多时候都在研究室里闷头度过，待在这里的时间少之又少。还记得当时为了不被侍女发现，特地拉上床帘准备瞒天过海……","transcript_en":"My room... I spent far less time here than I did in my study. That fact may have surprised my attendants, as I often closed the bed curtains to hide the fact I had once again slipped away to continue my research."},{"seq":47,"id":"vm_zelda_012","no":"No.012","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-995,"y":-379,"z":314,"gx":-379,"gy":995,"gz":314,"title_zh":"坚强的公主","title_en":"A Strong Princess","place_zh":"塞尔达公主的书房","place_en":"Princess Zelda's Study","transcript_zh":"我的研究室。我在荒废不堪的房间一角发现了宁静公主，她也许在地下等待了数年甚至数十年，只为破土而出的那一刻……你的坚强无人能及，我却曾说你是濒临灭绝的公主……真对不起","transcript_en":"My study... I found a silent princess in a corner of this desolate room... How many years—or decades—has it patiently waited for the right conditions, that it might finally emerge? To think I once believed the silent princess was doomed to extinction. You're stronger than anyone..."},{"seq":48,"id":"vm_zelda_013","no":"No.013","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-915,"y":-363,"z":284,"gx":-363,"gy":915,"gz":284,"title_zh":"昔日的露台","title_en":"Memories at the Gazebo","place_zh":"海拉鲁城堡凉亭","place_en":"Hyrule Castle Gazebo","transcript_zh":"这里曾是湛蓝屋顶的眺望台……达尔克尔调节着气氛，乌尔波扎给大家牵头……力巴尔总找机会和林克作对……米法会担心地看着他们两个……那段时光已经一去不复返，但我永远不会忘记我们在一起的点点滴滴。","transcript_en":"Among the many overlooks, this is my favorite. I remember spending time with Mother here. Back then, Father still laughed—frequently... I wonder if the day will come when we can laugh together like that again."},{"seq":49,"id":"vm_zelda_014","no":"No.014","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-430,"y":-247,"z":24,"gx":-247,"gy":430,"gz":24,"title_zh":"城邑的喷泉","title_en":"Castle Town Fountain","place_zh":"中央广场遗迹","place_en":"Central Square","transcript_zh":"中央广场遗迹。很久以前城邑就位于这里，虽然时间久远，但在我心里那热闹的城区历历在目，恍如昨日。喷泉的水应该是由地下的水道供应的……可能早就已经干涸了吧","transcript_en":"This is the center of Castle Town, otherwise known as Central Square. The fountain area is crowded with people and vendors—it's always so lively. The mood and scents here sometimes cause a wave of nostalgia in me, reminding me of the flower crown Mother bought me here when I was little."},{"seq":50,"id":"vm_zelda_015","no":"No.015","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-647,"y":78,"z":32,"gx":78,"gy":647,"gz":32,"title_zh":"大圣堂的回忆","title_en":"Cathedral Reminiscence","place_zh":"海拉鲁大圣堂遗迹","place_en":"Hyrule Cathedral","transcript_zh":"海拉鲁大圣堂遗迹。当初我为了觉醒封印之力，每天都会在此祈祷。这里让我倍感痛苦……也倍感温馨","transcript_en":"The ruins of Hyrule Cathedral... I often came here to pray that my powers would finally awaken... Though this place does bring me comfort, I also feel bitter at my many unanswered prayers..."},{"seq":51,"id":"vm_zelda_016","no":"No.016","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-360,"y":-244,"z":21,"gx":-244,"gy":360,"gz":21,"title_zh":"安魂的祈愿","title_en":"Requiem for the Dead","place_zh":"海拉鲁城邑遗迹","place_en":"Hyrule Castle Town Ruins","transcript_zh":"纪念碑。相传抱憾而终之人的灵魂会堕入深邃的地底，四处游荡寻求光明。于是我们决定在遇害最严重的地点设置了这块碑，祈祷此碑能够成为指引他们的光芒。","transcript_en":"A memorial... It is said that spirits who are weighed down with regret when they pass on sink deep beneath the ground and wander in search of light... I will place similar memorials at scenes of great loss and pray they will bring light to those wandering souls."},{"seq":52,"id":"vm_zelda_017","no":"No.017","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-811,"y":-675,"z":15,"gx":-675,"gy":811,"gz":15,"title_zh":"禁地","title_en":"Barred from the Prison","place_zh":"监狱遗迹","place_en":"Castle Town Prison","transcript_zh":"监狱遗迹。小时候大人们告诫我绝对不能跨过欧荷利桥，所以今天还是我第一次踏入这里。灾厄的业火席卷过后，徒留焦黑的梁柱……自那时起入狱的犯人早已不在，如今的海拉鲁想必不再需要监狱了。","transcript_en":"Beyond the moat bridge lies a prison where those who have committed grave crimes are sent. Ever since I was small, I have been forbidden to cross here."},{"seq":53,"id":"vm_zelda_018","no":"No.018","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1017,"y":-1267,"z":102,"gx":-1267,"gy":1017,"gz":102,"title_zh":"幸存之人的义务","title_en":"Our Responsibility","place_zh":"王室古代研究所遗迹","place_en":"Royal Ancient Lab Ruins","transcript_zh":"王室古代研究所遗迹。已经被破坏得惨不忍睹……普尔亚曾为失去大量文献和贵重样本而叹惋不已……还是从头来过吧。今后该由我们为后世留下历史了。","transcript_en":"This was once an impressive research site, but after being devastated by the Calamity, it is now known as the Royal Ancient Lab Ruins. Purah in particular has lamented the knowledge and samples that were lost here, but we can start again. It's our turn to build something we can leave to future generations."},{"seq":54,"id":"vm_zelda_019","no":"No.019","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1609,"y":-1667,"z":113,"gx":-1667,"gy":1609,"gz":113,"title_zh":"玛丽塔的纪念碑","title_en":"Maritta Memorial","place_zh":"玛丽塔交易所遗迹","place_en":"Maritta Exchange Ruins","transcript_zh":"据说曾有数不胜数的怪物在这平原横行肆虐。此地虽有幽深的山谷和利特族的守卫，但人们对外敌戒心薄弱，想必顷刻之间便沦陷了吧……愿逝者们的灵魂得到女神海利亚的指引……","transcript_en":"The land here has been trampled by monsters. With the deep valley nearby and the Rito already watching over the area, there seemed little need for additional protection. Unfortunately, that proved an incorrect assumption. I pray that those who lost their lives here found peace with Goddess Hylia..."},{"seq":55,"id":"vm_zelda_020","no":"No.020","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1776,"y":-1550,"z":106,"gx":-1550,"gy":1776,"gz":106,"title_zh":"移动的驿站","title_en":"Solitary Moving Stable","place_zh":"海拉鲁大森林","place_en":"Great Hyrule Forest","transcript_zh":"玛丽塔驿站。以前所有地方的驿站都会根据客流改变位置，但时至今日只有这座驿站会移动了。接下来要为了建造鸟望台新铺一条大路，听说他们要搬到那边去。这里的人们为搬家忙前忙后，等他们闲下来时再来打扰吧。","transcript_en":"I've been told the people of Serenne Stable just moved here, hence the many wooden boxes all around. Originally, stables were started up by nomadic people who would host travelers—it seems the tents at these stables are a relic of such times. Nowadays, stables stay put, so finding a mobile one such as this is a rare thing."},{"seq":56,"id":"vm_zelda_021","no":"No.021","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-3122,"y":226,"z":174,"gx":226,"gy":3122,"gz":174,"title_zh":"沉眠于黑暗的遗迹","title_en":"Slumbering Ruins","place_zh":"德依布朗遗迹","place_en":"Thyphlo Ruins","transcript_zh":"德依布朗遗迹。或许是因为神庙消失、试练不复存在，笼罩这里的黑暗不知何时已然散去。之所以能留下如此大规模的遗迹，想必是因为处在黑暗之中，外力无法介入。现在终于可以正式展开调查了。","transcript_en":"The existence of a shrine has been confirmed here at Thyphlo Ruins. Could that darkness act as a test to the one chosen by the sword that seals the darkness? I don't think I can go much farther, however. I wonder if I will have to ask him to come investigate? No, I don't want to have to rely on him for this."},{"seq":57,"id":"vm_zelda_022","no":"No.022","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-3749,"y":1554,"z":100,"gx":1554,"gy":3749,"gz":100,"title_zh":"化石调查的收获","title_en":"Importance of Fossil Studies","place_zh":"奥尔汀大化石","place_en":"Eldin Great Skeleton","transcript_zh":"奥尔汀大化石。海拉鲁地质调查工作依然没有进展。通过调查化石……理应可以知晓生物灭绝的原因……以及环境发生过怎样的变化……也许还能让我们防患于未然。今后最好多向化石调查方面投入一些努力。","transcript_en":"The Eldin Great Skeleton... Geological surveys of Hyrule have largely been at a standstill, but they could be incredibly valuable! Through careful study, we could identify extinction events and their causes... We could see evidence of environmental changes or disasters and possibly prevent them from happening again! And this all ties back to fossils. We simply must put more effort into their study."},{"seq":58,"id":"vm_zelda_023","no":"No.023","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2725,"y":-1033,"z":-78,"gx":-1033,"gy":2725,"gz":-78,"title_zh":"忘却神殿","title_en":"Forgotten Temple","place_zh":"忘却神殿","place_en":"Forgotten Temple","transcript_zh":"据古文献记载，海拉鲁有一座以初代王后命名的神殿，曾作为民众的避难所使用。时至今日历经无数战争，内部几乎完好无损……如果这座神殿利用地势，特意建造得格外坚固的话……说不定","transcript_en":"These ruins are thought to date back to the kingdom's founding. It seems likely that something of great value was once here, as there are many Guardians in the area. Additionally, according to ancient documents, there was a room beyond the Goddess Statue, but it now appears to be buried in sediment."},{"seq":59,"id":"vm_zelda_024","no":"No.024","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-3535,"y":-962,"z":234,"gx":-962,"gy":3535,"gz":234,"title_zh":"以北洛美之名","title_en":"Bearing the Name North Lomei","place_zh":"北洛美城堡遗迹","place_en":"North Lomei Labyrinth","transcript_zh":"北洛美城堡遗迹。这里的环境极其恶劣，构造犹如迷宫……怎么看都不像是一座普通城堡。考虑到这里曾存放着为被驱魔之剑选中之人准备的古代遗物，也有可能是一处试练之所。如果要深入调查，恐怕只有林克能胜任。","transcript_en":"The North Lomei Labyrinth is a harsh environment and an unsurprisingly labyrinthine structure... It has high walls but is otherwise unlike most fortifications. It did once hold an ancient relic meant for the bearer of the sword that seals the darkness, so perhaps it was a trial or test of some kind? I may just have to ask Link to investigate..."},{"seq":60,"id":"vm_zelda_025","no":"No.025","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-3571,"y":-3414,"z":367,"gx":-3414,"gy":3571,"gz":367,"title_zh":"明弗拉的秘泉","title_en":"Goflam's Secret Hot Spring","place_zh":"戈弗拉姆的秘密温泉","place_en":"Goflam's Secret Hot Spring","transcript_zh":"深山的秘泉。我一路循着动物的叫声，发现了一匹受伤的马儿。它可能正在温泉中养伤吧。我本来准备去北岳调查传闻中的大化石，可这匹马儿特别亲人，我走到哪里它跟到哪里。所以我决定先找个地方把它收容起来。总之得先找个驿站……","transcript_en":"A hot spring hidden deep within the mountain. I heard the pained cries of an animal and have now found an injured horse soothing its wounds in the refreshing waters. I had meant to investigate the immense skeleton on the northern summit, but this horse seems so friendly... Oh, the skeleton isn't going anywhere. Now how far away is the nearest stable..."},{"seq":61,"id":"vm_zelda_026","no":"No.026","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2572,"y":-1645,"z":233,"gx":-1645,"gy":2572,"gz":233,"title_zh":"金黄色的马","title_en":"The Golden Horse","place_zh":"雪原驿站","place_en":"Snowfield Stable","transcript_zh":"雪原驿站。我在调查途中发现了一匹受伤的马，就把它牵到了这座驿站，拜托店员为它疗伤。我本想带它一起上路，但又不能干等着它养好伤……于是我在它的鬃毛上按母后教的方法做了祈愿，希望它能遇到一个好主人。","transcript_en":"I came upon an injured horse and brought it to Snowfield Stable to be treated. I had hoped to bring it with me on my travels, but it needed more time to recover, so instead I offered a prayer that some kindhearted person would come to care for it. I may have also said a prayer—one I learned from Mother—to help with its mane."},{"seq":62,"id":"vm_zelda_027","no":"No.027","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1770,"y":-3244,"z":118,"gx":-3244,"gy":1770,"gz":118,"title_zh":"咖罗的烦恼","title_en":"Galli's Worries","place_zh":"白诘报社","place_en":"Lucky Clover Gazette","transcript_zh":"利特驿站。驿站主人咖罗先生似乎正为这座驿站的前途而烦恼。听说报社提出了收购这座驿站的申请。报社和驿站都是这个国家不可或缺的组织，真希望他们能商实现共存……","transcript_en":"I spoke with Galli at Rito Stable, who seems worried about whether he can keep the stable open, though it sounds like he's had an offer to sell it to a newspaper, of all things... In any case, Hyrule is all the better with newspapers and stables; maybe the two can find a way to coexist here."},{"seq":63,"id":"vm_zelda_028","no":"No.028","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1804,"y":-3302,"z":121,"gx":-3302,"gy":1804,"gz":121,"title_zh":"翔天之翼","title_en":"Wings Soaring the Skies","place_zh":"利特村","place_en":"Rito Village","transcript_zh":"100年前，风之神兽瓦·梅德就在这片天空中悠然翔。力巴尔得意洋洋地说，最会驾驭神兽的肯定是我，对吧？”可他的羽毛总是凌乱不堪……他强硬的话语每时每刻都在激励着我，因为我知道他付出了常人难以想象的努力。","transcript_en":"A hundred years ago, the Divine Beast Vah Medoh soared through the sky, and the Rito Champion, Revali, was ever quick to celebrate his skill as its pilot. Many may have been put off by his bravado, but I found it encouraging; there were often subtle signs that he was someone who worked hard, unseen, to be certain he could back up his bluster."},{"seq":64,"id":"vm_zelda_029","no":"No.029","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1836,"y":-3485,"z":153,"gx":-3485,"gy":1836,"gz":153,"title_zh":"追念力巴尔","title_en":"Honoring Revali","place_zh":"村前鱼塘","place_en":"Fishpond in Front of the Village","transcript_zh":"力巴尔……在我难过时……你总是第一个赶到我身边，可在你需要帮助时，我却没能伸出援手，实在是对不起……不过以你的性格，我猜你肯定会说“100年不过是眨眼的事”……你以前总是对林克鸡蛋里挑骨头，其实也是在替我发声，对不对？","transcript_en":"Revali... You were always quickest to rush to my side when I struggled. I'm sorry I wasn't able to help you when you were in need. You being you, I imagine you shrugged off waiting a hundred years like it was the smallest inconvenience... You were so tough on Link to make sure he could protect me, weren't you?"},{"seq":65,"id":"vm_zelda_030","no":"No.030","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1817,"y":-3571,"z":167,"gx":-3571,"gy":1817,"gz":167,"title_zh":"他的名字……","title_en":"His Name...","place_zh":"利特村","place_en":"Rito Village","transcript_zh":"利特村。利特英杰力巴尔的故乡。他的名字成为了传说，他的弓代代相传，由利特族当下最强的战士持有。你以前总是不喜欢别人谈论自己……但不好意思，以后你的事迹要一直在这里被人议论啦，力巴尔……","transcript_en":"Ah, Rito Village. Hometown of Revali, the Rito Champion. It seems he is spoken of as a legend here, and his bow is an honor bestowed on the best Rito warrior. You did hate other people talking about you, Revali, but I'm afraid your story will live on here for quite some time still..."},{"seq":66,"id":"vm_zelda_031","no":"No.031","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1803,"y":-3604,"z":213,"gx":-3604,"gy":1803,"gz":213,"title_zh":"力巴尔广场","title_en":"Revali's Landing","place_zh":"力巴尔广场","place_en":"Revali's Landing","transcript_zh":"以力巴尔的名字命名的广场。以前这里并没有名字……据说大灾厄降临那天，力巴尔就是从这里乘上神兽的。脚下地面的纹理和100年前一模一样，正说明人们从未懈怠过对这里的维护。想必是出于对利特族最强战士的敬意吧。","transcript_en":"This plaza has been named after Revali. It's said that he boarded the Divine Beast from here the day the Calamity began, and for that reason, and in his honor, it was given its name. The fact that the design on the ground has been carefully maintained and unchanged for a hundred years shows the immense respect the village holds for their legendary warrior."},{"seq":67,"id":"vm_zelda_032","no":"No.032","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1827,"y":-3626,"z":218,"gx":-3626,"gy":1827,"gz":218,"title_zh":"未来的族长","title_en":"The Future Elder","place_zh":"卡昂的家","place_en":"Kaneli's House","transcript_zh":"利特族族长卡昂。他告诉我他打算将族长的位子让给特巴。他曾认为战士和族长是不可兼顾的身份，但看到特巴和林克并肩冲向梅德的身姿，便确信特巴无论身为战士还是族长，都足以领导利特族走向未来。","transcript_en":"Kaneli, the village elder of the Rito, told me that he intends to pass his role on to Teba. He hadn't believed that a single Rito could serve both as the elder and the protector of the village at the same time. But when he saw Link and Teba face Medoh... Needless to say, he has no concerns whether the Rito will be in good hands with Teba."},{"seq":68,"id":"vm_zelda_033","no":"No.033","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2316,"y":-3791,"z":161,"gx":-3791,"gy":2316,"gz":161,"title_zh":"备受崇敬的战士","title_en":"A Warrior to Aspire To","place_zh":"飞行训练场","place_en":"Flight Range","transcript_zh":"飞行训练场。力巴尔在利特族中似乎备受崇敬，大多数孩子都想成为一名弓箭手，在这个地方勤学苦练。他曾说这个训练场是为自己打造的，但心里肯定希望未来的子孙后代也能用得上。时至今日，他的心意似乎已经生根发芽。","transcript_en":"Many of the Rito aspire to be like Revali, and most of the children follow his example and practice with the bow. The Flight Range is where they do the majority of their training. Though he always claimed the practice range was only meant for him, he did strive to make a better world for future generations, and that dream lives on here."},{"seq":69,"id":"vm_zelda_034","no":"No.034","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2882,"y":-2832,"z":564,"gx":-2832,"gy":2882,"gz":564,"title_zh":"1万年前的痕迹","title_en":"Scar from 10,000 Years Ago","place_zh":"海布拉山山顶","place_en":"Hebra Peak","transcript_zh":"海布拉山。100年前我还只是将信将疑，现在已经可以有理有据地推测，这里的形状就是1万年前从城堡方向发射的射线所致。这座山明明一直在默默陈述这个事实，可我们却……等回去以后，立刻组建调查队吧。我们不能再忽视来自过去的线索了……","transcript_en":"When I look at the Hebra Mountains now, I can accept something I couldn't one hundred years ago; the energy blast that shaped the peak 10,000 years in the past indeed came from the castle. Perhaps these mountains were always trying to teach us about the past... I should put together a survey team to investigate and make sure we aren't missing any other such messages."},{"seq":70,"id":"vm_zelda_035","no":"No.035","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-441,"y":-3474,"z":278,"gx":-3474,"gy":441,"gz":278,"title_zh":"后悔与忏悔","title_en":"Regret and Repentance","place_zh":"古代石柱群","place_en":"Ancient Columns","transcript_zh":"古代石柱群。印象里这地方以前也有一座神庙……在我一腔热血研究遗物的那段时间……我总会挑人烟稀少的地方调查，可是无论到哪里，林克总能找到我……那时我对林克的态度还很刻薄……后来我就此事向他道歉，他表示并没有放在心上，不过……","transcript_en":"These ancient columns mark where a shrine once stood... Before the Calamity, when I was frantically searching ruins, I would often seek hard-to-reach places. Despite this, Link always managed to find me. I was so terrible to him then... And of course when I apologized for it later, he reassured me that he didn't mind. I regret putting him through that."},{"seq":71,"id":"vm_zelda_036","no":"No.036","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-552,"y":-2917,"z":169,"gx":-2917,"gy":552,"gz":169,"title_zh":"饲养员的忧虑","title_en":"Worries of a Caretaker","place_zh":"塔邦挞大桥驿站","place_en":"Tabantha Bridge Stable","transcript_zh":"塔邦挞大桥驿站。这座驿站是在大规模修桥梁时新建的。可工后不久桥梁就因灾厄遭到摧毁，间接导致了驿站的知名度低迷，驿站主人为此忧心。听说他想把一道需要黄油的料理推广成特产，于是开始养起了山羊……但好像为照顾这不熟悉的动物费尽了心血。","transcript_en":"Tabantha Bridge Stable was built when the Tabantha Great Bridge was repaired after many years of neglect. However, the bridge was destroyed during the Calamity and only recently reopened, so the manager here is worried that no one knows about his stable. He purchased some goats and is trying to develop a signature dish using goat-milk butter, but there are definitely some things he needs to learn about the animals..."},{"seq":72,"id":"vm_zelda_037","no":"No.037","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-883,"y":-2254,"z":110,"gx":-2254,"gy":883,"gz":110,"title_zh":"雷鸣不再的台地","title_en":"The Plateau Where Thunder Fell Silent","place_zh":"雷之台地","place_en":"Thundra Plateau","transcript_zh":"雷之台地。这里曾如它的名字一样雷鸣不断，让人敬而远之。现在雷云已经散去，景色安宁得让人难以置信。想当初这地方还有一座神庙，那些电闪雷鸣也许是为勇者准备的试练吧。","transcript_en":"Thundra Plateau was so named for the endless rolling thunder that used to echo across it. I was hesitant to even come here, but with the thunder gone, this place is...incredibly peaceful. I wonder if the thunder was connected to the shrine that was here before... Maybe it was some sort of test."},{"seq":73,"id":"vm_zelda_038","no":"No.038","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":695,"y":-1622,"z":140,"gx":-1622,"gy":-695,"gz":140,"title_zh":"学习需用心","title_en":"Learning to Have an Open Heart","place_zh":"撒丁公园遗迹","place_en":"Sanidin Park Ruins","transcript_zh":"撒丁公园遗迹。这附近是一片开阔的草原，以前林克总在这里教我骑马。我自认为马术还算厉害，所以一开始并不觉得他能教会我什么。但后来，我从他身上学会了马术以外的东西……那就是关怀他人的","transcript_en":"Link often used the vast meadows of the Sanidin Park Ruins to help me practice horse handling. I recall thinking there was little I could learn from him. After all, I am quite capable on horseback. However, it wasn't technique he was showing me but rather deeper lessons in compassion."},{"seq":74,"id":"vm_zelda_039","no":"No.039","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":342,"y":-2263,"z":344,"gx":-2263,"gy":-342,"gz":344,"title_zh":"樱花的渊源","title_en":"Spreading Cherry Blossoms","place_zh":"萨托利山","place_en":"Satori Mountain","transcript_zh":"萨托利山的樱花。人们一直相当重视樱花，认为它可以除邪气。曾经世上只有两棵樱花树，但最近各地都能见到了。不知是因为邪气随灾厄消散，新的樱花树生根发芽……还是因为出现了新的邪气，需要除呢……？","transcript_en":"The Satori Mountain cherry blossom tree... While there were only two of these trees before, there seem to be many more now. However, it is said that cherry blossoms can purify evil... Does that mean more are appearing because the Calamity has disappeared, or are they appearing in preparation for some new threat?"},{"seq":75,"id":"vm_zelda_040","no":"No.040","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1274,"y":-1431,"z":32,"gx":-1431,"gy":-1274,"gz":32,"title_zh":"奇缘驿站","title_en":"The \"Meet-Up\" Stable","place_zh":"平原外围的驿站","place_en":"Outskirt Stable","transcript_zh":"平原外围的驿站。乌尔波扎告诉我，格鲁德族人把这里称作“奇缘驿站”，很多芭伊就是在这里第一次见到伯伊的。驿站里挂着的樱花地图说不定也是驿站主人的贴心设计。","transcript_en":"This stable is called Outskirt Stable, but the Gerudo apparently refer to it as the \"meet-up stable.\" Urbosa told me that this is where many vai see voe for the first time. Perhaps the stable master knows this, and that's why a map to cherry-blossoms—quite the romantic setting—is on display..."},{"seq":76,"id":"vm_zelda_041","no":"No.041","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2162,"y":-1581,"z":-22,"gx":-1581,"gy":-2162,"gz":-22,"title_zh":"环境恶劣的大地","title_en":"Harsh Lands","place_zh":"格鲁德峡谷入口","place_en":"Gerudo Canyon Pass","transcript_zh":"格鲁德峡谷入口。从干燥的岩石表面上不难看出这里的雨水有多么稀少。虽然还不至于非用耐暑药不可，但踏入此地便扑面而来的热气，会让我回想起穿过峡谷后的环境有多么恶劣。","transcript_en":"The dried rock face of the entrance to Gerudo Canyon shows how little rain this region gets. While it may not be so perilously hot as to require advanced elixirs, the sweltering air does strike you the moment you set foot here, and it serves as a warning of the rugged desert ahead."},{"seq":77,"id":"vm_zelda_042","no":"No.042","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2304,"y":-1956,"z":0,"gx":-1956,"gy":-2304,"gz":0,"title_zh":"瓦·娜波力斯的出土现场","title_en":"Vah Naboris Excavation Site","place_zh":"格鲁德峡谷","place_en":"Gerudo Canyon","transcript_zh":"这里是找到神兽瓦·娜波力斯的地点。据格鲁德英杰乌尔波扎所说，操控娜波力斯和她操控雷电的感觉颇为相似。只不过两者所需的意志力可谓是天差地别。","transcript_en":"This is where Divine Beast Vah Naboris was found. According to the Gerudo Champion, Urbosa, controlling the Divine Beast was similar in practice to how she controlled lightning. Both required considerable force of will, but with the Divine Beast, it was much, much more difficult."},{"seq":78,"id":"vm_zelda_043","no":"No.043","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2235,"y":-2789,"z":29,"gx":-2789,"gy":-2235,"gz":29,"title_zh":"怪物扎根的水井","title_en":"Monsters in the Well","place_zh":"格鲁德峡谷驿站","place_en":"Gerudo Canyon Stable","transcript_zh":"格鲁德峡谷驿站。这里的井中发现了怪物。我用岩石堵住了怪物的巢穴，但并非长久之计……为了不让此事引起恐慌，我告诫驿站主人暂时先不要使用这口井。尽管会带来不便，但眼下安全第一。","transcript_en":"There have been reports of monsters in the well here at Gerudo Canyon Stable, and though we have sealed the entrance of their den with rocks, I doubt that is a permanent solution... As an additional measure, I have also told the stable manager to avoid using the well. It will be inconvenient, but safety is of the highest priority."},{"seq":79,"id":"vm_zelda_044","no":"No.044","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2322,"y":-2934,"z":32,"gx":-2934,"gy":-2322,"gz":32,"title_zh":"格鲁德沙漠","title_en":"Gerudo Desert","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠入口","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Gateway","transcript_zh":"不知道是不是我的错觉……吹在脸上的风似乎比以前更热了一些。有人会把这里戏称为不毛之地，但我却觉得没什么地方比沙漠更能让人感受到生命力。也许是因为我亲眼见识了那些在恶劣的环境下顽强生存的人们……","transcript_en":"It may be my imagination, but it feels like there is even more heat in the air here than in the past. And despite that oppressive heat and the seemingly desolate environment, I believe there is more vitality in this desert than anywhere else. Perhaps I feel this way because I have seen the strength of those who call this place home."},{"seq":80,"id":"vm_zelda_045","no":"No.045","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2521,"y":-3211,"z":23,"gx":-3211,"gy":-2521,"gz":23,"title_zh":"绿洲蜃景","title_en":"Desert Oasis","place_zh":"卡拉卡拉集市","place_en":"Kara Kara Bazaar","transcript_zh":"卡拉卡拉集市。这里有士兵驻扎，建立了警卫体制。100年前，这个地方只有商人，并没有站岗的卫兵，就连我造访这里的时候都是乌尔波扎亲自担任护卫。现在似乎在露珠的调遣下加强了守卫。","transcript_en":"Kara Kara Bazaar serves as a trading post for those who cannot enter Gerudo Town. It's a smart thing, since the town only allows women to enter. Urbosa warned me to be on alert for the Yiga Clan here, but I cannot imagine they would attack in a place as crowded as this. She worries a bit too much."},{"seq":81,"id":"vm_zelda_046","no":"No.046","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2896,"y":-3817,"z":44,"gx":-3817,"gy":-2896,"gz":44,"title_zh":"年幼的族长","title_en":"The Young Chief","place_zh":"格鲁德小镇","place_en":"Gerudo Town","transcript_zh":"格鲁德小镇。由族长露珠领导的格鲁德族村落。她年纪虽小，却为族长职务鞠躬尽瘁，在神兽和依盖队的威胁之下，仍将小镇治理得比以前更有生气。相比之下，母后亡故时我却在一味哭泣，实在自愧不如……","transcript_en":"The main settlement of the Gerudo, Gerudo Town, is ruled by Chief Riju. Though young, she seems to be working hard in service to her people, overcoming both the Divine Beast and the threat the Yiga Clan posed. In fact, the town is more lively than ever! It is...humbling to see her face such challenges. When Mother died, I was inconsolable..."},{"seq":82,"id":"vm_zelda_047","no":"No.047","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2956,"y":-3877,"z":50,"gx":-3877,"gy":-2956,"gz":50,"title_zh":"谒见露珠","title_en":"An Audience With Riju","place_zh":"王宫王座厅","place_en":"Royal Palace's Throne Room","transcript_zh":"现任族长露珠。她本有一头只有王族才能留到及腰的长发，却不加迟疑地挥刀剪短。据她所说，此举一是表达自己的自责未能亲手保护民众免受神兽和依盖队侵袭，二是表明自己的决心一—要在头发再次及腰前成为像乌尔波扎一样强大的族长。","transcript_en":"The current chief of the Gerudo, Riju, used to have long hair reaching all the way to her waist—a style only permitted to Gerudo royalty. Today, however, she wears it cut short. I believe this is both in penance for not being able to stop the Divine Beast or the Yiga Clan on her own, but also to give herself a goal to aspire to. By the time her hair grows long again, she must be a strong chief like Urbosa was."},{"seq":83,"id":"vm_zelda_048","no":"No.048","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2987,"y":-3855,"z":43,"gx":-3855,"gy":-2987,"gz":43,"title_zh":"帕特丽夏","title_en":"Patricia","place_zh":"王宫庭院","place_en":"Palace Courtyard","transcript_zh":"露珠心爱的沙海象，帕特丽夏。据说是由她母亲所赠，在露珠埋头勤学和特训的时候一直陪在她身边。或许正因为朝夕相处，她们在不知不觉间便能互相沟通了。反正我肯定做不到这种事","transcript_en":"Riju's beloved sand seal, Patricia, was apparently a gift from her mother. They seem to have formed a close bond over the many years of Riju's studies and training. I...think they can even communicate with one another, though I am not able to understand Patricia at all."},{"seq":84,"id":"vm_zelda_049","no":"No.049","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2916,"y":-3899,"z":43,"gx":-3899,"gy":-2916,"gz":43,"title_zh":"格鲁德士兵强化计划","title_en":"Gerudo Soldier Training","place_zh":"兵舍","place_en":"Barracks","transcript_zh":"士兵的驻地。我听说露珠打算加强士兵的战斗力，但成果并不理想。于是我把乌尔波扎说过的话告诉给了她，“守护沙漠的第一步应该是统治沙漠。”露珠听后似乎想到了什么主意，死盯着地图好一段时间。乌尔波扎的话语无论在哪个时代都能指引人们前行。","transcript_en":"These are the barracks for Gerudo soldiers. Riju recently spoke of wanting to improve the training her soldiers receive, sharing, too, how she has been frustrated with the results so far. Hearing this, I told her of how Urbosa always felt the Gerudo should be more in touch with the desert. A look of realization crossed Riju's face, and then she spent some time studying a map. It seems Urbosa can offer wise guidance even a hundred years later."},{"seq":85,"id":"vm_zelda_050","no":"No.050","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2929,"y":-3765,"z":43,"gx":-3765,"gy":-2929,"gz":43,"title_zh":"沙海象的回忆","title_en":"Memories of the Sand Seals","place_zh":"沙海象租赁店东门分店","place_en":"Sand-Seal Rental Shop East Gate Booth","transcript_zh":"我驾驭沙海象的技术得到了露珠夸赞，这离不开过去乌尔波扎对我的特训。有一次我忘了带盾，结果被沙海象和乌尔波扎甩得远远的，自己站在原地不知所措。露珠听了这个故事，不禁捧腹大笑。哪怕到了现在，有时候我仍然无法相信，眼前这个绽放着天真笑容的孩子是一名族长。","transcript_en":"Riju complimented my technique when handling a sand seal, a skill I only possess thanks to the training Urbosa gave me so long ago. I then told Riju of the time I forgot a shield and was left behind by both my sand seal and Urbosa, and the young girl doubled over laughing! I still sometimes forget that this \"young girl\" is chief of her people."},{"seq":86,"id":"vm_zelda_051","no":"No.051","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2860,"y":-3857,"z":46,"gx":-3857,"gy":-2860,"gz":46,"title_zh":"时隔100年再度挑战","title_en":"Another Attempt, 100 Years Later","place_zh":"高贵酒馆","place_en":"The Noble Canteen","transcript_zh":"芭伊遇上伯伊。格鲁德小镇的招牌鸡尾酒。这次她们又拿“小姑娘喝这个还太早了”拒绝了我……听说不久后会有新的孩子搬到这个小镇，她们为了让这些孩子尽快融入这里，正在研制一种水果做的果汁。她们让我到时候再过来。","transcript_en":"I tried once again to get the popular Gerudo Town drink, Noble Pursuit, and I was once again told I was not ready for it yet. They did tell me I should come back when the young Gerudo children who have been living abroad return to town. Apparently some special drinks will be prepared for their arrival, and I should ask again then..."},{"seq":87,"id":"vm_zelda_052","no":"No.052","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2507,"y":-3762,"z":32,"gx":-3762,"gy":-2507,"gz":32,"title_zh":"不为人知的遗迹","title_en":"Mysterious Ruins","place_zh":"北格鲁德遗迹","place_en":"North Gerudo Ruins","transcript_zh":"北格鲁德遗迹。露珠悄悄告诉我说，这座遗迹实际上与格鲁德小镇地下相通，在必要的时候可以当作逃生通道。她笑着说，只要没出现什么天地异变级别的大灾难，肯定是用不上的。从那含笑的双眼中，我感受到了她保卫小镇和平的坚定决心。","transcript_en":"The North Gerudo Ruins are connected to Gerudo Town via an underground pathway that Riju showed me. She told me it was an escape route in the event of an emergency, but that short of some immense disaster, she couldn't imagine using it for such a purpose. She laughed as she said this, and though she seemed unconcerned in the moment, it's clear the safety of her people is never far from her mind."},{"seq":88,"id":"vm_zelda_053","no":"No.053","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1929,"y":-3661,"z":118,"gx":-3661,"gy":-1929,"gz":118,"title_zh":"深穴所通之处","title_en":"Exploring Where the Chasm Leads","place_zh":"比利丁高地的深穴","place_en":"Birida Lookout Chasm","transcript_zh":"比利丁高地的深穴。根据记录表明古代人生活在地底……我猜测这个深穴可能就通往地底，不过如此规模的调查工作需要委派专业的调查团队。找时间去问问普尔亚有没有合适人选吧。","transcript_en":"This is the chasm located near Birida Lookout... There are records that suggest ancient people lived far below ground in the Depths, and I suspect holes such as this one could connect the surface to that place... But if I want to find evidence proving my theories, I will need researchers wholly dedicated to the task. I should speak with Purah to see if she knows anyone qualified and capable of tackling this..."},{"seq":89,"id":"vm_zelda_054","no":"No.054","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3115,"y":-3422,"z":84,"gx":-3422,"gy":-3115,"gz":84,"title_zh":"沙漠中的哨所","title_en":"Desert Watchtower","place_zh":"瞭望台","place_en":"Lookout Post","transcript_zh":"哨所。原本是为监视神兽瓦·娜波力斯而建造的，现如今用来监视沙漠中的异常。据说建在这么高的地方就不会受到沙尘暴影响了。露珠还下令在卡拉卡拉集市修建灯塔，想必未来在沙漠旅行会轻松许多。","transcript_en":"This lookout post was supposedly originally built to keep watch on Divine Beast Vah Naboris as it lumbered through the desert, but now it is a place to observe changes in the desert landscape. I've heard it is tall enough to see above the worst sandstorms, and between this place and the lighthouse Riju has planned for Kara Kara Bazaar, safely traveling the desert should become easier soon."},{"seq":90,"id":"vm_zelda_055","no":"No.055","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3840,"y":-4857,"z":-21,"gx":-4857,"gy":-3840,"gz":-21,"title_zh":"化石考察的收获","title_en":"Concerning the Fossils","place_zh":"格鲁德大化石","place_en":"Gerudo Great Skeleton","transcript_zh":"格鲁德大化石。有研究表明太古时代的海拉鲁是沉在海底的。全世界出土的海洋生物化石也在佐证这一观点……可我总觉得，如果这个假说成立，化石的数量未免有些太少了……有没有可能是通过诸如比利丁高地的深穴等途径逃进地底的呢不……还是不要以假设为前提继续提出假设为妙……","transcript_en":"The immense Gerudo Great Skeleton lies here. Legends say that long, long ago, Hyrule was actually the bottom of a vast ocean. Considering the marine fossils that have been found across the world, I see little reason to doubt this. Except...it seems to me that there are too few fossils. Maybe sea life found routes even deeper? Maybe through chasms like the one near Birida Lookout? Maybe as far as the Depths... No, I'm getting carried away."},{"seq":91,"id":"vm_zelda_056","no":"No.056","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3331,"y":-1794,"z":72,"gx":-1794,"gy":-3331,"gz":72,"title_zh":"以南洛美之名","title_en":"Bearing the Name South Lomei","place_zh":"南洛美城堡遗迹","place_en":"South Lomei Labyrinth","transcript_zh":"南洛美城堡遗迹。海拉鲁共有3处以洛美命名的遗迹，由于构造复杂、环境恶劣，每一座我们都尚未踏足。它们也许是遥远古代流传下来的遗物，所以最好派遣专业的调查队进入。","transcript_en":"South Lomei Labyrinth is one of three ruins in Hyrule that have been named after Lomei. Each are incredibly complex in design and present harsh environments, which make them very difficult to explore. That said, they may contain important ancient relics, so it would be best to send out a dedicated survey team here."},{"seq":92,"id":"vm_zelda_057","no":"No.057","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2562,"y":-2053,"z":367,"gx":-2053,"gy":-2562,"gz":367,"title_zh":"追念乌尔波扎","title_en":"Honoring Urbosa","place_zh":"眼镜岩","place_en":"Spectacle Rock","transcript_zh":"乌尔波扎……我终于能够见到你眼中的景色了。时至今日，你丧命一事……还是令我无比内疚。但多亏有你……有大家留下的教诲，还有我们共同度过的时光，我才能在今天昂首挺胸活下去。谢谢你……我不会有事的。请把同样的话也转达给我的母后吧。","transcript_en":"I finally get to see all these amazing sights you saw, Urbosa. I wish that it hadn't cost what it did... But thanks to the things you—and everyone else—taught me, and the time we spent together, I can move forward with my head held high. Thanks to you, I am going to be OK... Could you tell my mother that for me, please?"},{"seq":93,"id":"vm_zelda_058","no":"No.058","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1506,"y":-578,"z":19,"gx":-578,"gy":-1506,"gz":19,"title_zh":"驿站村的纪念碑","title_en":"Outpost Memorial","place_zh":"门前驿站村遗迹","place_en":"Gatepost Town Ruins","transcript_zh":"这一带曾有数座旅馆，前往时之神殿朝圣之人、驻军地的士兵们来来往往，人声鼎沸。如今站在这里，耳边却只剩下风声……愿逝者们的灵魂得到女神海利亚的指引……","transcript_en":"This area was once alive and bustling with activity. There were several inns nearby, and the roads were busy with soldiers from the local garrison or travelers heading for the Temple of Time. Nowadays, only the wind moves through this place... I pray everyone who passed through here has found peace with Goddess Hylia."},{"seq":94,"id":"vm_zelda_059","no":"No.059","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1497,"y":-539,"z":18,"gx":-539,"gy":-1497,"gz":18,"title_zh":"海拉鲁的建国之地","title_en":"Birthplace of Hyrule","place_zh":"门前驿站村遗迹","place_en":"Gatepost Town Ruins","transcript_zh":"初始台地。入口被沙土和岩石堵住了。尽管部分地方在守护者的侵略下有所坍塌，但迹象表明岩石是从外面人为放置的，多半是为了防止其他怪物继续入侵才堵了起来。看来当初不止我一个人相信沉睡在复苏神庙的林克最终会醒来……我该从哪里进去呢……？","transcript_en":"The passage up to the Great Plateau has been filled with dirt and rocks. Certainly some of this damage was caused by the Guardians' invasion, but some of the debris looks to have been placed deliberately. I imagine the intention was to keep as many monsters as possible from reaching the Great Plateau, where Link recovered in the Shrine of Resurrection. But...how am I supposed to reach the Great Plateau now?"},{"seq":95,"id":"vm_zelda_060","no":"No.060","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1907,"y":-1125,"z":129,"gx":-1125,"gy":-1907,"gz":129,"title_zh":"勇者苏醒","title_en":"The Hero Awakened","place_zh":"修复室","place_en":"Restoration Room","transcript_zh":"复苏神庙。维持林克生命的古代希卡族遗物就曾放置于此。我清楚地感知到了，他从100年的长眠中醒来的那一刻。幸好……让他听到了我的声音……","transcript_en":"It was here in the Shrine of Resurrection that ancient Sheikah technology preserved Link's life. I was able to clearly sense when he woke from his hundred-year slumber, and I am so happy that my voice could reach him..."},{"seq":96,"id":"vm_zelda_061","no":"No.061","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2004,"y":-818,"z":116,"gx":-818,"gy":-2004,"gz":116,"title_zh":"沧海桑田","title_en":"The Passage of Time","place_zh":"时之神殿遗迹","place_en":"Temple of Time Ruins","transcript_zh":"时之神殿。古文献中也能找到对它的记录，但文献中描述的模样和我们如今见到的外形相去甚远。这是海拉鲁漫长历史中的一项未解之谜。","transcript_en":"There are several ancient texts and works of literature that speak of the Temple of Time by name, but all of them describe a structure that differs in design from the one we see today. Hyrule's history is long, and this discrepancy is one of the unsolved mysteries of our land..."},{"seq":97,"id":"vm_zelda_062","no":"No.062","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2216,"y":-1291,"z":311,"gx":-1291,"gy":-2216,"gz":311,"title_zh":"必须守护之物","title_en":"A King's Rest","place_zh":"王之墓","place_en":"King's Tomb","transcript_zh":"父王的坟墓。听说当时把石头堆成墓费了不少力气……这个地方能够眺望海拉鲁大地，想必是对父王最好的祭奠了。父王，母后……此时此刻，放眼望去仍是一片百废待兴的景象，但我保证……一定会重现我们当年一同欣赏的美景……请二位在天之灵保佑我吧","transcript_en":"Father's grave. I heard that stacking these rocks was the best that could be done for him... Well, they could not have picked a better place. That he will rest here, forever looking out over Hyrule... Mother, Father, though the land is still littered with ruins, I promise you that I will restore it. Please... watch over me as I do."},{"seq":98,"id":"vm_zelda_063","no":"No.063","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2256,"y":-788,"z":88,"gx":-788,"gy":-2256,"gz":88,"title_zh":"小屋的主人是……","title_en":"The Hut's Owner","place_zh":"老人的小屋","place_en":"Old Man's Cabin","transcript_zh":"山间小屋。以前造访这里时，因为不知道屋主去了哪里，小屋还摇摇欲坠，我便提议将其拆除，结果父王露出了复杂的表情……有些苦……又有些感伤……难道这间小屋的主人是父王……？从这小屋的造型来看，大概是他亲手搭建的吧","transcript_en":"When I last visited this mountain hut a hundred years ago, I did not realize who the owner was. Now that I do, it explains why Father looked so troubled—even sad—when I described the building as \"shabby\" and in need of demolition. How could I have guessed it was his own little retreat... Though, looking at it now... Oh, Father, did you build this yourself?"},{"seq":99,"id":"vm_zelda_064","no":"No.064","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1672,"y":-1181,"z":83,"gx":-1181,"gy":-1672,"gz":83,"title_zh":"林克的心理阴影","title_en":"Link's Trauma","place_zh":"青蛙池塘","place_en":"Hopper Pond","transcript_zh":"青蛙池塘。不知道是不是因为怪物肆虐，曾经俯拾皆是的速速青蛙几乎都看不到了……我好不容易抓住一只想递给林克看看，可他却和我保持距离不肯靠近，真是莫名其妙。亏我还想","transcript_en":"Hopper Pond used to be filled with hot-footed frogs... Perhaps the monsters have driven them away? In any case, this is the place I finally managed to catch one. I was incredibly excited, and I tried to show Link, but he kept flinching and backing away from me..."},{"seq":100,"id":"vm_zelda_065","no":"No.065","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":565,"y":-591,"z":22,"gx":-591,"gy":-565,"gz":22,"title_zh":"不灭尊严","title_en":"Unshaken Bravery","place_zh":"海拉鲁驻军地遗迹","place_en":"Hyrule Garrison Ruins","transcript_zh":"海拉鲁驻军地遗迹。当初这里也遭到了大量守护者进攻。然而绝大部分士兵都已派往海拉鲁各地，据说都没有像样的武器拿来防守，仅剩不多的将士们拿着士兵之剑、士兵之枪拼死抵抗。","transcript_en":"The Hyrule Garrison ruins... As with other fortified locations, many Guardians attacked this place. However, it is likely most of the soldiers normally stationed here had already been deployed to other regions. Those few who remained fought bravely, though they were certainly ill-equipped to deal with such deadly foes."},{"seq":101,"id":"vm_zelda_066","no":"No.066","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":439,"y":-1108,"z":64,"gx":-1108,"gy":-439,"gz":64,"title_zh":"腐朽的千年古树","title_en":"Ancient Tree Stump","place_zh":"腐朽的千年古树","place_en":"Ancient Tree Stump","transcript_zh":"千年古树。经考古学家调查，腐朽的树干内部发现了一杆疑似来自古代的枪。听说这一历史性重大发现引起了不小的轰动。具体由来目前尚不清楚，学者之间似乎也议论纷纷。","transcript_en":"In Hyrule, there are a number of large, decaying trees that are likely over one thousand years old, not unlike this tree stump. There is a legend about this tree in particular that says it was inhabited by a dignitary spirit. I, too, sense something important from this tree. An archaeological survey will soon take place here, so I cannot wait to hear about their findings."},{"seq":102,"id":"vm_zelda_067","no":"No.067","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-97,"y":-253,"z":8,"gx":-253,"gy":97,"gz":8,"title_zh":"忐忑不安","title_en":"Precautions on Top of Precautions","place_zh":"避难壕","place_en":"Emergency Shelter","transcript_zh":"观测瘴气的据点。在我表示要和林克一起前往城堡地下调查后，遭到了普尔亚的强烈反对。这里有一条和城堡连通的密道，我在此安设了一处据点，以便在突发情况时逃离。普尔亚这才勉强答应了我的请求。","transcript_en":"When I told Purah of my plan to venture beneath the castle to investigate the gloom, she expressed... strong opposition. That Link would accompany me did not sway her in the slightest. It was only my suggestion to establish an outpost here—a place to observe the gloom from and to reach the hidden path beneath the castle—that earned her begrudging acceptance."},{"seq":103,"id":"vm_zelda_068","no":"No.068","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-130,"y":-285,"z":19,"gx":-285,"gy":130,"gz":19,"title_zh":"招募！测量员！","title_en":"Surveyors Wanted!","place_zh":"监视堡垒 鸟望台","place_en":"Lookout Landing Skyview Tower","transcript_zh":"鸟望台。出于复兴需要，委托了普尔亚研发测量大地的装置。目前仍在建设之中，但在松达建筑店的帮助下，建设进度突飞猛进。听说还需要一名会用滑翔帆的人从空中测量，但好像没有一个人自告奋勇……","transcript_en":"This is one of the Skyview Towers that Purah designed to aid in the restoration of Hyrule. Though it is not quite finished, we have Hudson Construction to thank for how quickly it is coming along. Now if only Purah could have similar success finding any volunteers to use the paraglider to survey the land from above..."},{"seq":104,"id":"vm_zelda_069","no":"No.069","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-150,"y":-234,"z":26,"gx":-234,"gy":150,"gz":26,"title_zh":"调查队成立","title_en":"Assembling the Survey Team","place_zh":"研究所","place_en":"Research Lab","transcript_zh":"我们可以从历史中学到许多。比如应对灾厄的准备也是建立在研究古代遗物之上的……我在旅途中感受到了许多考古学家的热情，于是决定组建一支研究遗迹和古文献的调查队。古人留下的信息一定会为复兴工作带来益处。","transcript_en":"There are many things we can learn from history. After all, we would not have known to prepare for the Calamity if we had not studied ancient relics from our past. Knowing this, and having seen the passion of the archaeologists I have met on my travels, I have decided to form a team to survey ancient ruins and texts across Hyrule. I am sure there are many things we can learn from them as we restore the land."},{"seq":105,"id":"vm_zelda_070","no":"No.070","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":40,"y":-270,"z":19,"gx":-270,"gy":-40,"gz":19,"title_zh":"建材放置场","title_en":"Materials Cache","place_zh":"鸟鸣草原","place_en":"Passeri Greenbelt","transcript_zh":"虽说修复大路和桥梁是当务之急，但眼下并没有充足的人手。为此我们决定在各地设置了人人都可以取用材料的建材放置场。除了松达建筑店外，驿站协会也提供了帮助，实在对他们感激不尽。","transcript_en":"It is critical that we repair Hyrule's roads and bridges. Unfortunately, despite the efforts of Hudson Construction and the Stable Association, we lack the labor to tackle this task. We are blessed with abundant resources, however, so we've established material caches dedicated to the rebuilding efforts and made them freely available."},{"seq":106,"id":"vm_zelda_071","no":"No.071","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":217,"y":-63,"z":23,"gx":-63,"gy":-217,"gz":23,"title_zh":"牛奶色的黄昏","title_en":"Flavor Memories","place_zh":"麦贝镇遗迹","place_en":"Mabe Village Ruins","transcript_zh":"麦贝镇遗迹。这里曾是离城堡最近的牧场，因此我偶尔会乔装前来拜访，这里的人们总会热情款待我，美味的食物叫人应接不暇……他们都把动物当成自己的家人一般，恐怕当时不会有人愿意独自逃命……","transcript_en":"The ruins of Mabe Village... It was the farm closest to the castle, and I would often visit it incognito. They always shared far more food than I could possibly eat, and I remember that they treated their animals like members of their family. I imagine no one here fled alone when the time came..."},{"seq":107,"id":"vm_zelda_072","no":"No.072","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-801,"y":245,"z":21,"gx":245,"gy":801,"gz":21,"title_zh":"春风吹又生","title_en":"New Sprouts","place_zh":"海拉鲁森林公园遗迹","place_en":"Hyrule Forest Park","transcript_zh":"王族直辖的森林公园，由历代国王们长久植树打造而来。如今已有一部分被烧毁，但仍能看到嫩芽新生。看来祖先们的心意一直流传到了今天。","transcript_en":"This forest park was the direct responsibility of the royal family, cared for and built upon by each successive generation of rulers. Though it has been partially destroyed by fire, that does not spell the end of our ancestors' legacy. In fact, I believe I caught sight of some new growth emerging already."},{"seq":108,"id":"vm_zelda_073","no":"No.073","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1243,"y":720,"z":33,"gx":720,"gy":1243,"gz":33,"title_zh":"劳鲁村落的纪念碑","title_en":"Rauru Settlement Memorial","place_zh":"劳鲁村落遗迹","place_en":"Rauru Settlement Ruins","transcript_zh":"尽管演习场的士兵们奋力迎战，仅仅一台守护者便让这个村落瞬间陷入火海，人们甚至没有逃生的时间……加之这一带地基不稳，如今已是面目全非……愿逝者们的灵魂得到女神海利亚的指引","transcript_en":"Although the soldiers at the training camp fought back, this settlement was burned to the ground by a single rampaging Guardian. The loose ground has left little trace of the heroic battle they waged... I pray their brave spirits have found peace with Goddess Hylia."},{"seq":109,"id":"vm_zelda_074","no":"No.074","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1145,"y":1042,"z":22,"gx":1042,"gy":1145,"gz":22,"title_zh":"驿站的乐团","title_en":"The Stable Trotters","place_zh":"森林驿站","place_en":"Woodland Stable","transcript_zh":"森林驿站。听说驿站协会会长的孙子组建了一个乐团。他挥舞指挥棒的动作……还有点……生硬。不过，可能是他那欢快的模样吸引了其他人，据说接二连三地招到了几个成员。等调查结束，就来这里好好欣赏一下吧。","transcript_en":"I'll always remember Woodland Stable. It is where I saw the president of the Stable Association's grandson swinging a baton around. It seems he has formed a band, gathering one musician after another. While his mannerisms are clumsy, others are enthralled by his appearance and enthusiasm. Once I have finished my investigation, I should try to see them perform."},{"seq":110,"id":"vm_zelda_075","no":"No.075","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1382,"y":858,"z":103,"gx":858,"gy":1382,"gz":103,"title_zh":"为士兵们祈福","title_en":"A Prayer for Brave Soldiers","place_zh":"海拉鲁军事演习场遗迹","place_en":"Military Training Camp","transcript_zh":"海拉鲁军事演习场遗迹。精兵们早已被派往各地，大灾厄来临之日，驻扎在此的大多是还在训练的士兵。据说他们齐心协力才勉强和1台守护者同归于尽……愿这些勇敢的士兵能够安息……","transcript_en":"This was an important training camp in the days before the Calamity. It is said that when the Calamity occurred, all of the veteran soldiers had been deployed and only trainees remained here. Despite their inexperience, the brave trainees worked together and defeated a Guardian. I pray their souls have found peace..."},{"seq":111,"id":"vm_zelda_076","no":"No.076","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1620,"y":1603,"z":289,"gx":1603,"gy":1620,"gz":289,"title_zh":"新的道路","title_en":"A New Route","place_zh":"鼓大湖","place_en":"Goronbi Lake","transcript_zh":"这一带曾经满是熔岩，连靠近都难如登天。如今火山不再喷发，海利亚人不用做好耐热措施也可以直接进入了，所以才在这附近修建了新的道路。道路两侧还建起了店铺，这里的客流变化也是天翻地覆。","transcript_en":"This area used to be covered in lava and was largely unapproachable, but now that the volcanic eruptions have subsided, even Hylians can come here without taking fire-resistance measures. Thus, the new path! I've heard there are even plans for new shops along the road; this place is about to see some significant changes."},{"seq":112,"id":"vm_zelda_077","no":"No.077","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2434,"y":1613,"z":387,"gx":1613,"gy":2434,"gz":387,"title_zh":"食岩饕客","title_en":"Rock Connoisseurs","place_zh":"鼓隆城","place_en":"Goron City","transcript_zh":"鼓隆城。我带了好多防火药过来，但现在好像不需要了……不过鼓隆族们还是在津津有味地吃着岩石。我记得以前达尔克尔还请林克吃过岩石来着……现在回想起来还是忍俊不禁。","transcript_en":"When I was preparing to come here to Goron City, I bought lots of fireproof elixirs to counter the extreme heat. It's a relief to see those are no longer needed. One thing that hasn't changed, though, is the Gorons' love of eating rocks. Seeing it now, I am reminded of when Daruk gave Link a rock to eat... and he did!"},{"seq":113,"id":"vm_zelda_078","no":"No.078","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2394,"y":1709,"z":395,"gx":1709,"gy":2394,"gz":395,"title_zh":"重叠的身影","title_en":"A Familiar Visage","place_zh":"鼓隆城","place_en":"Goron City","transcript_zh":"我来到达尔克尔家登门拜访，想要见见他的后代。那时我看到个名叫沅的年轻人。他的体型和达尔克尔如出一辙，甚至在看到背影时，我下意识叫了一声“达尔克尔”。这个年轻人虽然没有达尔克尔的勇武，但有一颗朴实而温柔的心……","transcript_en":"I was surprised when I first saw Yunobo. The young Goron is built just like his grandfather, and I nearly shouted \"Daruk!\" in excitement. Of course, he doesn't have the same bold spirit Daruk had, but he is an honest boy with a truly kind heart."},{"seq":114,"id":"vm_zelda_079","no":"No.079","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2469,"y":1662,"z":386,"gx":1662,"gy":2469,"gz":386,"title_zh":"肌肉亭","title_en":"Peak Protein Provisions","place_zh":"鼓隆美食店","place_en":"Goron Gusto Shop","transcript_zh":"石头烧烤料理店。听说为了在新修建的道路旁开餐馆，这家店要关门了。他们似乎找到了一个手艺了得的烧烤师傅，准备把餐馆交给他打理。由于临近关门，店家还免费请我吃了烤兽肉。","transcript_en":"This restaurant specializes in grilling various foods, though it seems they are planning on leaving this location to a skilled chef and opening a new shop along the road. Since they were moving on, they were kind enough to give me a seared steak as a gift."},{"seq":115,"id":"vm_zelda_080","no":"No.080","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2505,"y":1695,"z":397,"gx":1695,"gy":2505,"gz":397,"title_zh":"私人锻造师","title_en":"Blacksmith on Retainer","place_zh":"鼓隆城","place_en":"Goron City","transcript_zh":"达尔克尔扛在肩上的大剑。碎岩巨剑是他专门订制的武器，别看他平时拿放自如，实际上重量足有一般大剑的两倍左右。听说在他成为英杰以后，又将它加重了几分，用以锻炼自身。他勇武的表面下是沉重的责任心，从武器上也同样看得出来。","transcript_en":"This blacksmithing shop doesn't seem to have a name. I get the sense that the blacksmith himself is more concerned with his skills than he is about naming things. Truly, he is a master at his craft—his stature both grand and indomitable. Without so much as a momentary pause while striking the iron, he proudly told me that he was the very one who made Daruk's Boulder Breaker."},{"seq":116,"id":"vm_zelda_081","no":"No.081","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2409,"y":1665,"z":458,"gx":1665,"gy":2409,"gz":458,"title_zh":"追念达尔克尔","title_en":"Honoring Daruk","place_zh":"鼓隆桥","place_en":"Stolock Bridge","transcript_zh":"达尔克尔……林克向我转述了你在灵魂得以解放前所说的话。真抱歉，让你直到最后一刻都在为我们担心……谢谢你履行100年前的承诺……今后该由我接过这一棒了。我向你保证，我们定会实现你所展望的和平……请你见证下去吧。","transcript_en":"Oh, Daruk... Link told me of when your spirit was released. I am so sorry that you worried after me all the way to the end, and I cannot thank you enough for keeping the promise you made a hundred years ago. I will make you proud, my friend. I will bring peace to this land. Please...watch over me."},{"seq":117,"id":"vm_zelda_082","no":"No.082","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2326,"y":2169,"z":526,"gx":2169,"gy":2326,"gz":526,"title_zh":"平息的火山","title_en":"A Slumbering Volcano","place_zh":"奥尔汀桥","place_en":"Bridge of Eldin","transcript_zh":"死亡之山。过去熔岩从火山口喷涌而出，现如今已经彻底平息。听说古代的鼓隆族，曾有一段时期栖居在死亡之山的地底……也许现在这样才是这座山本来的面貌……","transcript_en":"It was not long ago that lava was frequently and fiercely erupting from Death Mountain. These days, the mountain seems to have quieted though. Hmm... I've heard stories that ancient Gorons built dwellings far down in the depths of the mountain. I wonder if this is similar to how the mountain looked back then."},{"seq":118,"id":"vm_zelda_083","no":"No.083","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2822,"y":1608,"z":423,"gx":1608,"gy":2822,"gz":423,"title_zh":"改善风气的阿沅","title_en":"Yunobo Is Making the World Better","place_zh":"阿沅队本部","place_en":"YunoboCo HQ","transcript_zh":"死亡之山的剧变让许多鼓隆族茫然无措，但阿沅依旧每天坚持前往荒山，兢兢业业地开采矿石。据说他这勤恳的态度让支持他的人日益增多。想必他会为鼓隆城的前途带来一片光明。","transcript_en":"The sudden changes on Death Mountain left many Gorons feeling uneasy, but I hear young Yunobo goes to the mountain every day to mine ore from the exposed rock face. It seems his efforts are motivating his fellow Gorons, shaking them out of their worry and giving them purpose... Certainly the future of Goron City is brighter thanks to Yunobo."},{"seq":119,"id":"vm_zelda_084","no":"No.084","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2243,"y":1774,"z":477,"gx":1774,"gy":2243,"gz":477,"title_zh":"违反规矩","title_en":"Accidentally Ill-Mannered","place_zh":"鼓隆温泉","place_en":"Goron Hot Springs","transcript_zh":"鼓隆温泉。看到鼓隆族泡得那么舒服，我也试着泡了泡脚。这一带的温泉水温都很高，林克刚想往里面加点水，就被鼓隆族警告了。对他们来说，现在的温度还不够热吧。","transcript_en":"The Gorons looked so comfortable as they lounged in these hot springs... As for me, the heat was too much, and I only put my feet in. Poor Link even caught a scolding from the Gorons when he tried to add a little water to cool it down; apparently this temperature is merely tepid to them already."},{"seq":120,"id":"vm_zelda_085","no":"No.085","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1132,"y":2597,"z":147,"gx":2597,"gy":1132,"gz":147,"title_zh":"文武双全的教诲","title_en":"Train Mind and Body","place_zh":"山麓驿站","place_en":"Foothill Stable","transcript_zh":"驿站是情报的宝库。调查队员的身影也越来越多了。调查队刚成立不久，我们就已经收到来自各地的调查报告，这都离不开他们的努力。不过，调查总是伴随着危险……我觉得有必要给调查员们传授一些防身的本领。","transcript_en":"Stables are a treasure trove of information and a great place to find members of the research team. Though we've only just begun our work, we've already received research reports from every region. As we continue working, I should ensure they know how to defend themselves... Exploring the unknown can be dangerous, after all."},{"seq":121,"id":"vm_zelda_086","no":"No.086","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1233,"y":2431,"z":116,"gx":2431,"gy":1233,"gz":116,"title_zh":"封闭的登山口","title_en":"Blocked Trailhead","place_zh":"死亡之山登山口","place_en":"Maw of Death Mountain","transcript_zh":"这里以前是死亡之山的登山口，如今却因道路崩塌、怪物盘踞，鲜有旅行者的身影……如果达尔克尔在，区区怪物早就被他一扫而空了……嗯……只要对手是怪物的话……","transcript_en":"This was previously the trailhead for Death Mountain, but the path has collapsed, and monsters have descended on the area, scaring off most of the travelers. If Daruk were here, I'm sure he'd clear out any opposition in no time. Assuming there are no dogs among them..."},{"seq":122,"id":"vm_zelda_087","no":"No.087","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1372,"y":3048,"z":285,"gx":3048,"gy":1372,"gz":285,"title_zh":"阿卡莱堡垒的纪念碑","title_en":"Akkala Citadel Memorial","place_zh":"阿卡莱高原","place_en":"Akkala Highlands","transcript_zh":"人们曾称这座堡垒“坚不可摧”……这份傲慢令我们付出了代价……未来我们必须从阿卡莱堡垒战役中吸取教训，抬头向前走……我向此碑发誓，必将复兴海拉鲁、恢复世间和平，决不能让逝者们白白牺牲。","transcript_en":"We thought Akkala Citadel impregnable, but the battle here proved it was anything but... We must carry the lessons learned from this battle forward with us. I vow to honor the sacrifices of those who died here—I will work tirelessly to restore Hyrule and to create a peaceful future for its people."},{"seq":123,"id":"vm_zelda_088","no":"No.088","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1679,"y":3131,"z":201,"gx":3131,"gy":1679,"gz":201,"title_zh":"守护者所到之处","title_en":"Path of the Guardians","place_zh":"南阿卡莱驿站","place_en":"South Akkala Stable","transcript_zh":"南阿卡莱驿站。守护者的铁蹄一度经过此地，尽管建筑悉数遭毁，但听说工作人员都成功逃出生天。想必是阿卡莱堡垒的士兵们为他们争取了时间吧……驿站协会动员所有人投入重建工作，如今已经完全看不出当年的惨烈。","transcript_en":"South Akkala Stable... Many, many Guardians swept through this area, and though the building was destroyed, the workers were all able to get to safety. No doubt that is thanks to the soldiers of Akkala Citadel buying them time... But now the Stable Association has rebuilt the stable, and you can hardly see any traces of the past destruction."},{"seq":124,"id":"vm_zelda_089","no":"No.089","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2286,"y":3044,"z":334,"gx":3044,"gy":2286,"gz":334,"title_zh":"不为人知的夏特","title_en":"The Lost Hamlet","place_zh":"夏特村落遗迹","place_en":"Shadow Hamlet Ruins","transcript_zh":"夏特村落遗迹。这个与世隔绝的村子不与其他村落来往，村民的下落无人知晓之前我来传达灾厄的警告时被他们拒于门外，倘若我再坚持一些，是否会有不同的结局呢","transcript_en":"No one actually knows what happened here at the Shadow Hamlet during the Calamity. They were a very isolated village, and they liked it that way. They even turned me away when I came to warn them about the Calamity. I wonder if this place would be more than ruins if I had tried harder to get them to listen..."},{"seq":125,"id":"vm_zelda_090","no":"No.090","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2656,"y":3745,"z":3,"gx":3745,"gy":2656,"gz":3,"title_zh":"是正是邪","title_en":"Good and Evil","place_zh":"力量之泉","place_en":"Spring of Power","transcript_zh":"力量之泉。这里尽管还留有些许泉水，但因无人问津而荒废不堪。如今肯定还有很多人将力量视为魔王的象征，因此十分忌讳。但力量本身没有错，是掌控力量的人决定了它是正是邪。","transcript_en":"Though the Spring of Power remains, it has been neglected and fallen into ruin. I imagine many see power as a symbol of the Demon King and thus avoid the spring, but there is a misunderstanding there. Power itself is neither inherently evil nor good; it is the individual wielding that power that defines it."},{"seq":126,"id":"vm_zelda_091","no":"No.091","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2732,"y":4239,"z":125,"gx":4239,"gy":2732,"gz":125,"title_zh":"特产 赈灾包子","title_en":"The Signature Steamed Buns","place_zh":"东阿卡莱驿站","place_en":"East Akkala Stable","transcript_zh":"东阿卡莱驿站。这里最早是一处避难所，是由驿站协会从各个驿站搜罗各种废弃材料，为战火中流离失所的人们打造的。当时为赈灾制作的包子，如今已是这座驿站的特产了。","transcript_en":"Apparently, East Akkala Stable got its start when the Stable Association used scrap wood left over from other stables to construct a shelter for people whose homes had burned down. The kitchen prepared steamed buns for the people then, and the recipe has become a signature meal here."},{"seq":127,"id":"vm_zelda_092","no":"No.092","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-3144,"y":4505,"z":245,"gx":4505,"gy":3144,"gz":245,"title_zh":"天才们的执着","title_en":"Particular Geniuses","place_zh":"阿卡莱古代研究所","place_en":"Akkala Ancient Tech Lab","transcript_zh":"阿卡莱古代研究所。据说普尔亚和洛贝利在被守护者摧毁的废灯塔上重修了一处研究所。虽然他们给出的理由是这里遗留着许多值得研究的古代遗物，但我猜他们为了避免自己研究的东西再次伤害到他人……故意选了远离人烟的地方","transcript_en":"The Akkala Ancient Tech Lab was originally a lighthouse Guardians destroyed. Apparently, Purah and Robbie later converted it into a lab. They claim its proximity to ruins is why they chose this place, but I think the real reason they settled here was to discourage visitors. Their research was dangerous, after all..."},{"seq":128,"id":"vm_zelda_093","no":"No.093","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1620,"y":4023,"z":127,"gx":4023,"gy":1620,"gz":127,"title_zh":"理想世界","title_en":"An Ideal World","place_zh":"一始村","place_en":"Tarrey Town","transcript_zh":"一始村。这个村子是围绕松达先生，跨越种族隔建立起来的。听说林克也出了一份力……这里不止有海利亚人，还有利特族、鼓隆族、卓拉族、格鲁德族共同安居乐业。我所展望的复兴后的世界，就在这里得以一窥。","transcript_en":"Tarrey Town, a village that brought all the peoples of Hyrule together. Hudson is the driving force behind its founding, though they say Link played a role as well. Hmm... This place—where Hylians, Rito, Goron, Zora, and Gerudo all live together in peace—is a model of the world I hope to see in the future."},{"seq":129,"id":"vm_zelda_094","no":"No.094","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1593,"y":3941,"z":128,"gx":3941,"gy":1593,"gz":128,"title_zh":"寡言的社长","title_en":"Taciturn President","place_zh":"一始村","place_en":"Tarrey Town","transcript_zh":"松达建筑店。松达先生正在四处奔波，为重建工作寻找工匠，似乎大部分时间都不在店里。听说他快要当爸爸了，尽管他一向沉默寡言，但也看得出他坐立难安的心情。","transcript_en":"Hudson Construction... It seems Hudson is rarely in the shop, as he is busy recruiting workers for the restoration efforts. I hear he is expecting a child soon, and though he is a reserved man, I can see his quiet excitement."},{"seq":130,"id":"vm_zelda_095","no":"No.095","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1600,"y":3924,"z":128,"gx":3924,"gy":1600,"gz":128,"title_zh":"“达”的老规矩","title_en":"Successor \"Son\"","place_zh":"一始村","place_en":"Tarrey Town","transcript_zh":"松达建筑店继承了其前身——樱达建筑店的方针，员工的名字最后一个字必须是“达”才行。唯一一个名字里没有“达”的是哈吉先生，他在面试的时候说了自己叫“哈吉”，却被听成了“哈吉达”，所以得到了录用……","transcript_en":"They say Hudson Construction adopted the name policy from its predecessor, Bolson Construction; all employees must have a name that ends in \"son.\" There is technically one exception though. A man named Hagie supposedly introduced himself as \"Hagie, son\" in his interview, which Hudson mistook for \"Hagieson.\""},{"seq":131,"id":"vm_zelda_096","no":"No.096","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1606,"y":3911,"z":129,"gx":3911,"gy":1606,"gz":129,"title_zh":"危险的载具","title_en":"A Less-Than-Safe Ride","place_zh":"一始村","place_en":"Tarrey Town","transcript_zh":"从村子前往作业场所的交通工具。听说是利用高低差一路滑到底的轨道车……结构非常简单，就只是一根绑着滑轮的吊绳。又因为是单向的，回村时就得从外面绕一大圈。如果能用上希卡族科技，会不会更方便些呢……","transcript_en":"This track facilitates transit from the village to the work area. It is not a complex creation, relying on the height difference to send the rope and pulley down the rails. However, it is only one way, so a person would have to walk back along the perimeter to reach the village. Hmm... I wonder if Sheikah technology could improve this..."},{"seq":132,"id":"vm_zelda_097","no":"No.097","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1608,"y":3769,"z":89,"gx":3769,"gy":1608,"gz":89,"title_zh":"松达建筑店作业场所","title_en":"Hudson Construction Workshop","place_zh":"松达建筑店 作业场所","place_en":"Hudson Construction Site","transcript_zh":"塔林湿地水位下降，露出了地表。这似乎就是松达建筑店的作业场所选址此地的原因之一。复兴所用的建材似乎都是在此生产并送往各地的。不知道以后这里会发展成什么样子呢。","transcript_en":"Apparently, when the water levels in Torin Wetland receded and solid ground emerged, Hudson Construction decided to build a workspace here. That workspace has come to be the main site for producing the building materials used in our restoration efforts. I'm excited to see how this place flourishes."},{"seq":133,"id":"vm_zelda_098","no":"No.098","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1484,"y":3662,"z":89,"gx":3662,"gy":1484,"gz":89,"title_zh":"士兵们的奇策","title_en":"Cunning Tactics","place_zh":"塔林湿地","place_en":"Torin Wetland","transcript_zh":"塔林湿地。据说这里曾有大量守护者的残骸，不过如今已是荡然无存。扎堆在一处的守护者丧失了机动性优势，攻击也难免会误伤彼此……阿卡莱地区受害较轻，想必得归功于城堡士兵们的足智多谋吧。","transcript_en":"Torin Wetland was once littered with the broken remains of countless Guardians, though there are no longer any traces of them. I imagine the wetlands reduced the Guardians' mobility, making it impossible for them to avoid each other's attacks. No doubt Akkala owes thanks to the quick thinking of soldiers from the citadel for this. If the Guardians hadn't been so hindered, the Akkala region would have suffered more damage."},{"seq":134,"id":"vm_zelda_099","no":"No.099","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":41,"y":3257,"z":234,"gx":3257,"gy":-41,"gz":234,"title_zh":"镌刻的卓拉历史","title_en":"Inscriptions of Zora History","place_zh":"露朵山","place_en":"Ruto Mountain","transcript_zh":"卓拉石碑。以前上面铭刻的是多雷凡大王的话语，现在则换成了希多的。听说他让林克骑在自己的背上，一同对抗神兽卓拉族几乎不会把自己的背后交给他人，可见他对林克付出了全盘信赖。","transcript_en":"The Zora created these stone monuments, and while they once were engraved with the words of King Dorephan, they now bear those of Sidon. He has written of the battle against the Divine Beast, when he allowed Link to ride on his back. That really shows how completely he trusts Link; it is rare for a Zora to let anyone on their backs, after all..."},{"seq":135,"id":"vm_zelda_100","no":"No.100","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-276,"y":3530,"z":289,"gx":3530,"gy":276,"gz":289,"title_zh":"友谊之桥","title_en":"Building a Relationship","place_zh":"露朵台地","place_en":"Ruto Precipice","transcript_zh":"蓄水湖。这是一片由卓拉族和海拉鲁王国共同修建的人工湖，作用是预防河川泛滥。当时卓拉族和海拉鲁王国尚未建立牢固的友好关系，这片蓄水湖似乎成了两者之间的友谊之桥。","transcript_en":"In order to prevent the damage a flooding river would cause, the Zora people and the Kingdom of Hyrule worked together to build this reservoir. In fact, though they were only amicable toward each other before the project, it was the act of building this that formed a true friendship between the Zora and the Kingdom of Hyrule."},{"seq":136,"id":"vm_zelda_101","no":"No.101","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-262,"y":3207,"z":136,"gx":3207,"gy":262,"gz":136,"title_zh":"大灾厄的亲历者","title_en":"Those Who Remember the Calamity","place_zh":"卓拉大桥","place_en":"Great Zora Bridge","transcript_zh":"卓拉领地。卓拉族是长寿的种族，因此许多亲身经历大灾厄且认识米法本人的族人都还在世。我知道他们并不欢迎我的到来，但我必须要告诉他们……米法的经历","transcript_en":"Thanks to their long lifespans, many Zora here in Zora's Domain still remember the events of the Calamity and Mipha's part in all of it a hundred years ago. I do not think I will be welcomed, but it is my duty to tell them what happened to her in the end..."},{"seq":137,"id":"vm_zelda_102","no":"No.102","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-463,"y":3298,"z":139,"gx":3298,"gy":463,"gz":139,"title_zh":"米法雕像的转移","title_en":"Statue Relocation","place_zh":"卓拉领地广场","place_en":"Zora's Domain Square","transcript_zh":"100年前称颂英杰而建造的米法像，如今却成为了缅怀她的地方。听说是希多提议并将这座雕像搬到了视野开阔的特殊地点。","transcript_en":"A hundred years ago, a statue was made to celebrate Mipha, the Zora Champion. It is now a memorial to her sacrifice. Apparently it is thanks to Sidon that it stands where it does. It was he who proposed it be relocated to a place with a wonderful view."},{"seq":138,"id":"vm_zelda_103","no":"No.103","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-540,"y":3333,"z":164,"gx":3333,"gy":540,"gz":164,"title_zh":"谒见多雷凡大王","title_en":"Audience with King Dorephan","place_zh":"王座厅","place_en":"Throne Room","transcript_zh":"我和林克一起在聚集的卓拉族面前讲述了米法的经历。泣声和怒吼充斥着渴见室，而多雷凡大王像是要制止他们一般，平静地说了一句“谢谢”。他仿佛在告诉我们，不要沉于过去，而要抬头向前","transcript_en":"King Dorephan rules over the Zora and is father to Mipha. He's known for his incredible strength—in fact, he fights with his fins rather than wielding a weapon. One of the guards here even told me excitedly about an army of monsters who were eradicated with a single blow from the king."},{"seq":139,"id":"vm_zelda_104","no":"No.104","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-491,"y":3333,"z":140,"gx":3333,"gy":491,"gz":140,"title_zh":"少女的祈祷","title_en":"A Maiden's Prayer","place_zh":"铁锤商店","place_en":"Hammerhead","transcript_zh":"听说卓拉铠甲是为祈祷心上人的平安而打造的。据说米法曾多次来到这里，独自为林克制作出了这件铠甲。她可能是知道自已没有勇气亲手送给林克，所以才把它交给多雷凡大王保管的吧","transcript_en":"I have heard that an important part of the process of crafting Zora Armor is a prayer for the safety of a loved one. Apparently, Mipha often came to this place to work on armor she made for Link. However, in the end she left the armor with King Dorephan... Perhaps she knew she would not be able to hand it to Link herself."},{"seq":140,"id":"vm_zelda_105","no":"No.105","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-507,"y":3297,"z":140,"gx":3297,"gy":507,"gz":140,"title_zh":"鱼乡旅馆","title_en":"Seabed Inn","place_zh":"水底旅馆","place_en":"Seabed Inn","transcript_zh":"水床。我在100年前向旅店老板提出的荒诞设想，此时此刻竟然真的实现了。躺上去宛若在水中漂游，给人梦幻般的享受。这个水床不仅吸引了众多旅行者，在卓拉族之间也备受欢迎。","transcript_en":"The beds in the Zora inn are hard and apparently quite unpopular among travelers. The owner consulted with me about it, saying that since Zora sleep in the water, they aren't sure what makes a bed good or bad. I offered a suggestion of creating a bed that's akin to floating in water. That may have been too unrealistic..."},{"seq":141,"id":"vm_zelda_106","no":"No.106","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-591,"y":3642,"z":197,"gx":3642,"gy":591,"gz":197,"title_zh":"大王净身之所","title_en":"Kings' Purification Ceremony","place_zh":"清流王居","place_en":"Pristine Sanctum","transcript_zh":"清流王居。卓拉族的大王在让位后会隐居于此。历代大王用清流洗净身体，并将自已的鳞片放入这个宝座，象征着自己已经舍弃尘世。","transcript_en":"The Pristine Sanctum is part of the traditions a retiring Zora king follows upon abdicating their title. It is said that many generations of kings have cleansed their bodies in the pristine waters here, as well as offering one of their scales to this throne. In so doing, they symbolically abandon the earthly world."},{"seq":142,"id":"vm_zelda_107","no":"No.107","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-421,"y":3759,"z":539,"gx":3759,"gy":421,"gz":539,"title_zh":"追念米法","title_en":"Honoring Mipha","place_zh":"尝试海角","place_en":"Shatterback Point","transcript_zh":"米法……这个地方真美，放眼望去能看到整个领地。我把你最后的话语转告给了多雷凡大王，他对我说了句“谢谢”。该道谢的应该是我才对……真的很谢谢你……我也还想再多和你聊聊，","transcript_en":"I'm sure that you love the view of the village from here, don't you, Mipha? I shared your final words with King Dorephan, you know. He told me \"thank you.\" But I should be the one offering my thanks... and I do. I offer them to you. Thank you, Mipha. I wish only that we had more time together..."},{"seq":143,"id":"vm_zelda_108","no":"No.108","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":307,"y":1571,"z":10,"gx":1571,"gy":-307,"gz":10,"title_zh":"与马儿共存的村子","title_en":"The Horse-Rearing Village","place_zh":"科彭嘉村遗迹","place_en":"Goponga Village Ruins","transcript_zh":"科彭嘉村遗迹。这个村子曾将特殊的地形当作马既，养育了许许多多的马儿，但在怪物的摧残下，原来的景象几乎不复存在……但我相信……村民们都骑着马儿逃出了村子。","transcript_en":"Here in Goponga Village, they're working to make it possible to manage horses with just a few people. This would be achievable by using the small islands scattered about Lanayru Wetlands as stables. There's a grassy field at the village's entrance where the horses seem to be living at ease. And the villagers here even told me my white horse is beautiful."},{"seq":144,"id":"vm_zelda_109","no":"No.109","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":162,"y":894,"z":25,"gx":894,"gy":-162,"gz":25,"title_zh":"驿站协会","title_en":"The Stable Association","place_zh":"湿地驿站","place_en":"Wetland Stable","transcript_zh":"在驿站协会的提议下，所有驿站都安设了水井。在那场大灾厄中，守护者的猛烈攻击让地面之上变成了一片火海。我们吸取这一教训，在水井中留出了能安置人员的空间，紧急情况时不仅能保证用水，还能供人避难藏身。","transcript_en":"Father decided that the stables would be places of refuge in preparation for the Calamity. In his words, \"There is more to protecting our people than simply fighting.\" The Stable Association was thus established to further strengthen cooperation, and Mestro, proprietor of Wetland Stable, was appointed as its first chairman."},{"seq":145,"id":"vm_zelda_110","no":"No.110","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":832,"y":853,"z":10,"gx":853,"gy":-832,"gz":10,"title_zh":"笑靥如花","title_en":"Blooming Joy","place_zh":"花之中州","place_en":"Floret Sandbar","transcript_zh":"花之中州。我和以前在这里种花的奥可芭一起决定，要将这里打造成一片海拉鲁各种花儿绽放的花田。虽然找驿站借到了必要的农具，但因为不熟悉农活，搞得自己满身是泥。宁静公主……潜行草……大剑草……接下来要种点什么好呢","transcript_en":"The Floret Sandbar and Magda, who cultivates flowers here, inspired me to create a place where flowers from all over Hyrule could bloom together. Though I was able to borrow tools from a stable, I am not... adept at this kind of work. The dirt has gotten everywhere. Still, I must focus. Silent princess... Blue nightshade... Mighty thistle... What next?"},{"seq":146,"id":"vm_zelda_111","no":"No.111","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1082,"y":334,"z":9,"gx":334,"gy":-1082,"gz":9,"title_zh":"美食家云集的驿站","title_en":"Gathering of Gourmets","place_zh":"河畔驿站","place_en":"Riverside Stable","transcript_zh":"河畔驿站。这里因被称为“美食家云集的驿站而闻名。说起来……记得上次一群美食家说着什么“空腹是最佳的调料”，足足三天没吃东西，结果在帐篷里动弹不得，最后还是我给他们分了一些兽肉盖饭吃……但愿他们别再饿昏过去了","transcript_en":"Riverside Stable is known to many as a gathering place for gourmets. Visiting here reminds me of a time I shared a meal of meat and rice with a few who claimed \"hunger is the best sauce.\" Though at the time, they had not eaten in three days and were nearly immobilized at their campsite. I hope they learned their lesson..."},{"seq":147,"id":"vm_zelda_112","no":"No.112","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3438,"y":518,"z":47,"gx":518,"gy":-3438,"gz":47,"title_zh":"马术传道师","title_en":"Sharing the Joy of the Equestrian Arts","place_zh":"高原驿站","place_en":"Highland Stable","transcript_zh":"高原驿站。这里曾盛行骑射演武，但据说在大灾厄过后一不振……现在他们似乎在教旅行者如何驾驶马车，尽心尽力推广与马儿共同生活的方式。","transcript_en":"Ah, Highland Stable. Horseback archery was very popular before the Calamity, though it appears interest has waned in modern times. Instead, there is considerable effort being made to teach travelers how to handle horse-drawn wagons, and more importantly, how to care for the horses that pull them."},{"seq":148,"id":"vm_zelda_113","no":"No.113","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2384,"y":879,"z":18,"gx":879,"gy":-2384,"gz":18,"title_zh":"向龙展示勇气","title_en":"Courage Proven","place_zh":"勇气之泉","place_en":"Spring of Courage","transcript_zh":"勇气之泉。入口处的石像有一个传闻，叫作“无勇气者将为龙所噬”。以前我特别害怕，根本不敢踏入里面。其实也不止是小时候……我一直都对自己的勇气没什么信心，为此惶惶不安……但现在，我已经不会再瑟瑟发抖，一定可以彻查一番了。","transcript_en":"Long ago, I was too scared to enter the Spring of Courage... Not even just as a child, though then I could at least blame the intimidating message on the stone statue: \"Those who lack courage will be eaten by a dragon.\" But even as an adult, I always worried that I wasn't brave enough. Today, I think I can investigate every corner of this place without fear."},{"seq":149,"id":"vm_zelda_114","no":"No.114","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3520,"y":1550,"z":60,"gx":1550,"gy":-3520,"gz":60,"title_zh":"咚构","title_en":"Dondons","place_zh":"湖畔驿站","place_en":"Lakeside Stable","transcript_zh":"湖畔驿站。我们在密林深处发现了新物种，将其命名为了“咚构”并保护在这座驿站里。从它背上岩石般的凸起来看，它以前可能是靠拟态隐藏自己的……我打算和它一起生活一段时间，以便观察习性。","transcript_en":"Lakeside Stable is the closest stable to where I first discovered the creatures I have named Dondons. I found them deep in the jungle, and I knew I had to do what I could to protect them. I believe they use the rock-like bumps on their backs as a way to conceal themselves, but that is all I have learned so far. I think I will spend some more time observing them..."},{"seq":150,"id":"vm_zelda_115","no":"No.115","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3543,"y":2585,"z":184,"gx":2585,"gy":-3543,"gz":184,"title_zh":"如愿以偿","title_en":"A Wish Realized","place_zh":"恋人池","place_en":"Lover's Pond","transcript_zh":"这里被称为“爱之池”，是一片心形的水池。我记得以前应该没有这种地方……听说这里曾被称为祈愿山，有许多人前来造访……他们的愿望化为实体，形成了爱之池……这个说法难免令人发笑……但我还挺乐意相信的。","transcript_en":"I have heard stories about a heart-shaped pond, known as the Lover's Pond. I am almost certain it wasn't here before, although... This place was once thought of as the \"wish-making mountain,\" and I hear many people would visit. Perhaps all their wishes manifested as the pond? Some may laugh at this idea, but... I think I like it."},{"seq":151,"id":"vm_zelda_116","no":"No.116","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3602,"y":2561,"z":238,"gx":2561,"gy":-3602,"gz":238,"title_zh":"祈愿山","title_en":"Mountain of Prayers","place_zh":"卡尔山","place_en":"Tuft Mountain","transcript_zh":"卡尔山。以前曾是一座著名的结缘山，如今似乎鲜有人知道这个外号，因而无人问津。山顶的景色壮丽无比，想必眺望此景之时，内心的烦恼都会如沉入天边的夕阳一般消失得无影无踪。","transcript_en":"Tuft Mountain is a destination for many mountaineers. It's also known as the matchmaking mountain. The custom is to climb in total silence, and upon reaching the top, pray as the sun dips below the horizon. I set out to climb the mountain myself, but I was stopped by Link who observed how very steep it is. Personally, I feel he was being overly cautious."},{"seq":152,"id":"vm_zelda_117","no":"No.117","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3381,"y":2829,"z":2,"gx":2829,"gy":-3381,"gz":2,"title_zh":"款待","title_en":"Hospitality","place_zh":"沃托里村","place_en":"Lurelin Village","transcript_zh":"沃托里村。以前这里是一个渔村，听说海里的怪物多了起来，大部分村民都不再以捕鱼为生。如今这里已是一处让旅行者尽享美景和美食的度假胜地。村子虽然模样有变，人情味却一如既往……还是这个地方能让人抛却烦恼，安下心来。","transcript_en":"The cove here in Lurelin Village is so lively with its many boats. Even before anyone recognized who I was, I was treated with hospitality and warmth. The villagers served me a dish with an exquisite, vibrantly colored fish. You cannot find such a fish anywhere around the castle. Everyone here is so cheerful and kind... Spending time among them, I was able to forget the current hardships, even if momentarily."},{"seq":153,"id":"vm_zelda_118","no":"No.118","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3415,"y":2893,"z":6,"gx":2893,"gy":-3415,"gz":6,"title_zh":"228道料理","title_en":"Two Hundred and Twenty-Eight Recipes","place_zh":"拉聂尔湾","place_en":"Azure Bay","transcript_zh":"这里的一位太太请我吃了一道美味的料理，实在让我目结舌。她告诉我，她在结婚前环游海拉鲁，学会了足足228道料理。我建议她凭这手艺开一家餐厅，她嘴上笑着推辞，但好像也没有完全否认。","transcript_en":"I was amazed at the delicious food I was treated to by the fantastic cook here. It seems she traveled far and wide in Hyrule, gathering an incredible 228 recipes, before getting married and settling down. I suggested she open a restaurant, and while she seemed to laugh at the idea, I saw a quiet pride at the compliment."},{"seq":154,"id":"vm_zelda_119","no":"No.119","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3425,"y":2924,"z":2,"gx":2924,"gy":-3425,"gz":2,"title_zh":"船形的房子","title_en":"Ship-Shaped Shelter","place_zh":"海滨度假村","place_en":"Fishing Resort","transcript_zh":"外形像船的房子。据说这个房子是利用废弃船只建造的，固定船身时还用到了椰子树，如今已成为了这个村子的景点。可能是太大而不适合做民宅，现在村民把这里当作旅馆经营。","transcript_en":"It seems they turned an abandoned ship hull into a house, even using palm trees to hold the ship in place! It has become something of a local landmark, as well as a place for guests to stay. Considering its size, it really does make sense they would use it as an inn."},{"seq":155,"id":"vm_zelda_120","no":"No.120","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3443,"y":2920,"z":0,"gx":2920,"gy":-3443,"gz":0,"title_zh":"大海的守护神","title_en":"Guardian of the Ocean","place_zh":"沃托里村","place_en":"Lurelin Village","transcript_zh":"沃托里村的女神像。现在村民将其奉为大海的守护神。这座女神像原本是渔业的守护神，想必是因为渔民减少、日常生活方式转变，其作用也发生了变化。顺应时代变化生活下去并非易事，这个村子的人们身上有许多值得我们学习的地方。","transcript_en":"The goddess statue in Lurelin Village is now worshipped as the guardian of the ocean. I believe it used to be thought of as the guardian of fishing, but it seems that, as the number of fishers shrank here, the role of the goddess statue has changed along with the village itself. Hmm... Not everyone can adapt to the changes that life brings. There is much we can learn from the people of this village."},{"seq":156,"id":"vm_zelda_121","no":"No.121","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3638,"y":3794,"z":0,"gx":3794,"gy":-3638,"gz":0,"title_zh":"魔王的钩爪","title_en":"Demon King's Claw","place_zh":"伊萨奇海角","place_en":"Soka Point","transcript_zh":"克莱西亚半岛曾有“魔王的钩爪”的别称为村民们所忌禅，但现在似乎没人知道这个名字的由来。我一路走到半岛边缘，也并未感受到什么邪气。也许是有其他的原因吧","transcript_en":"Cape Cresia is commonly referred to as \"Demon King's Claw,\" but nobody seems to know the origin of that name. Areas where evil spirits gather occasionally experience unique topographical shifts. I find myself wondering if this is such a place..."},{"seq":157,"id":"vm_zelda_122","no":"No.122","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3656,"y":2964,"z":0,"gx":2964,"gy":-3656,"gz":0,"title_zh":"随浪而逝的天方夜谭","title_en":"A Wild Idea Lost to the Sea","place_zh":"科尔奈海滩","place_en":"Korne Beach","transcript_zh":"科尔奈海滩。沃托里村的村长向我征求意见，该如何让村子为更多人所知。这一带刚好没有珊瑚礁，所以我设想利用海域打造一些娱乐设施……但这想法太过天马行空，我实在说不出口。","transcript_en":"When the head of Lurelin Village asked me how he might raise awareness about his village, I immediately thought of this place. Korne Beach has such long stretches of sand, and it's free of coral reefs... I thought perhaps some sort of playground that incorporates the ocean would be a wonderful addition, but no, it really is an outlandish idea. I couldn't even bring myself to suggest it."},{"seq":158,"id":"vm_zelda_123","no":"No.123","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":3445,"y":4504,"z":0,"gx":4504,"gy":-3445,"gz":0,"title_zh":"尽头的岛屿","title_en":"Eventide Island","place_zh":"托隆波海滩","place_en":"Toronbo Beach","transcript_zh":"塞哈特诺岛。这里100年前被怪物占领而无人靠近，但在灾厄结束后，那些怪物似乎也几近消失。我们刚一登上岛屿，林克就捂住了自己的双眼，我便问他为什么这样做……结果他告诉我，以前在这里接受试练的时候，全身的衣服都被强行扒光了……这话倒是在捂眼之前跟我说啊","transcript_en":"A hundred years ago, Eventide Island was filled with monsters and impossible to safely approach. Link came along to protect me, but he suddenly covered his eyes the moment we landed. Fortunately, it seems all the monsters vanished with the Calamity... Regardless, when I asked him what he was doing, he said the last time he was here, he had been stripped of...ahem...all his possessions when he arrived. He...could have mentioned that possibility before I set foot on the shore..."},{"seq":159,"id":"vm_zelda_124","no":"No.124","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1874,"y":764,"z":14,"gx":764,"gy":-1874,"gz":14,"title_zh":"双子山的纪念碑","title_en":"Dueling Peaks Memorial","place_zh":"西哈特尔","place_en":"West Necluda","transcript_zh":"逃离城邑的民众人山人海，走到这里回头望去，却发现人数少了大半……双子山近在尺尺之际，守护者却出现在眼前，大家都以为要命丧于此……是你们挺身而出对抗强敌，让其他人得以逃命……谢谢你们。请安息吧……","transcript_en":"Many people evacuated from the town around Hyrule Castle, but less than half of them made it from there to this point... And even then, as they saw the Guardians appear before the Dueling Peaks, they thought they were done for. Thankfully, these brave souls were here to protect them. I pray they found peace at last."},{"seq":160,"id":"vm_zelda_125","no":"No.125","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1938,"y":1325,"z":12,"gx":1325,"gy":-1938,"gz":12,"title_zh":"救赎的双子","title_en":"Twin Saviors","place_zh":"双子山","place_en":"Dueling Peaks","transcript_zh":"双子山。如果不是林克带领大家来到这里，不知道后果会有多么严重……这里地形险峻，是抵御守护者的要冲，许多民众得以生还。当然也包括我在内……那时的我只有被别人保护的份……","transcript_en":"The Dueling Peaks... I shudder to think of what would have happened if Link hadn't lead everyone here. The steep terrain gave us some protection and plenty of places to hide from the Guardians. Many lives were saved, including my own. I was always being protected back then..."},{"seq":161,"id":"vm_zelda_126","no":"No.126","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1945,"y":2033,"z":18,"gx":2033,"gy":-1945,"gz":18,"title_zh":"悼亡之剑","title_en":"Grave Markers","place_zh":"克罗切利平原","place_en":"Blatchery Plain","transcript_zh":"克罗切利平原。一路走来的路上，我看到了许多替代墓碑仁立的剑……在这片无处可逃的平原上，守护者单方面的屠杀令许多士兵命丧于此……我们决不能遗忘他们的牺牲。","transcript_en":"The Blatchery Plain... Many soldiers lost their lives here when Guardians rampaged through the area. Now numerous swords throughout the field mark their graves. I passed by so many as I made my way here... It is our duty to never forget them nor the sacrifice they made."},{"seq":162,"id":"vm_zelda_127","no":"No.127","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1835,"y":2318,"z":11,"gx":2318,"gy":-1835,"gz":11,"title_zh":"哈特诺堡垒的纪念碑","title_en":"Fort Hateno Memorial","place_zh":"哈特诺堡垒","place_en":"Fort Hateno","transcript_zh":"有些人把哈特诺堡垒一役称作“奇迹”其实那根本不是什么奇迹……而是林克和无数士兵拼上性命守护了民众……如果我能更早觉醒力量，就不会……但愿逝者们的灵魂得到女神海利亚的指引","transcript_en":"Though some believe a miracle occurred here at Fort Hateno, the truth is less divine. We were all saved thanks to the soldiers, including Link, who chose to risk their lives here. Though they would not have had to do so if my power had awakened sooner. Regardless, I pray their spirits were comforted by Goddess Hylia."},{"seq":163,"id":"vm_zelda_128","no":"No.128","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1919,"y":1741,"z":10,"gx":1741,"gy":-1919,"gz":10,"title_zh":"伫立在激战地带的驿站","title_en":"The Stable on a Battlefield","place_zh":"双子驿站","place_en":"Dueling Peaks Stable","transcript_zh":"双子驿站……以前这里并没有驿站……也许应该说，还好没有驿站……这一带曾被守护者蹂躏，是整个海拉鲁受灾最为严重的地方……","transcript_en":"Dueling Peaks Stable is one of the newly established stables. Considering this whole area was devastated by the Calamity and completely overrun by Guardians, it's a good thing there was not a stable here before..."},{"seq":164,"id":"vm_zelda_129","no":"No.129","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1025,"y":1940,"z":130,"gx":1940,"gy":-1025,"gz":130,"title_zh":"隐秘 希卡族","title_en":"Hidden Sheikah Tribe","place_zh":"卡卡利科村","place_en":"Kakariko Village","transcript_zh":"卡卡利科村。住在此地的希卡族平日里和平生活，但在必要的时候也会拔剑战斗。这个村子之所以没有受到灾厄的侵害，应该是因为他们亲手消灭掉了怪物吧。","transcript_en":"Ah, Kakariko Village... The Sheikah that live here are quite peaceful, but that does not mean they are unwilling or unable to defend themselves. I would not be surprised if this village avoided the worst of the Calamity because any monsters that threatened it were summarily dealt with by the villagers themselves."},{"seq":165,"id":"vm_zelda_130","no":"No.130","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":984,"y":1784,"z":123,"gx":1784,"gy":-984,"gz":123,"title_zh":"百年友谊","title_en":"Hundred-Year-Old Friendship","place_zh":"族长宅邸","place_en":"Chief's Hall","transcript_zh":"我来到这里和100年前的朋友见了面。她以前是城堡的执政副官，大灾厄过后就任了族长，听说她一直在等待我的归来。看到我的时候，她的脸上浮现出了安心的表情，像是在说“我的任务终于完成了”。我们促膝长谈，仿佛要填满这100年未见的时光。","transcript_en":"I came here to visit a friend that I had not seen in a hundred years. She had been an advisor to the royal family, and following the Calamity, she became the leader of this village while awaiting my return. The relief on her face when she saw me... We talked for hours and hours, trying to make up for all the time we'd lost."},{"seq":166,"id":"vm_zelda_131","no":"No.131","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1010,"y":1790,"z":115,"gx":1790,"gy":-1010,"gz":115,"title_zh":"三色鲤鱼","title_en":"Sanke Carp","place_zh":"卡卡利科村","place_en":"Kakariko Village","transcript_zh":"瀑布潭中游着一种纹路独特的美丽鱼儿。这一定就是100年前那些研究者们在这里废寝忘食配种培育的观赏鱼。想必大灾厄让研究一度受挫，可他们还是坚持到了完成的那一天，真不愧是希卡族啊。","transcript_en":"There are beautiful fish with a unique patterning living in the waters beneath the falls... They must be the ornamental fish Sheikah researchers worked tirelessly to breed here a hundred years ago. Their efforts were certainly hindered by the Calamity, but it doesn't surprise me that the Sheikah would still find a way to finish their work."},{"seq":167,"id":"vm_zelda_132","no":"No.132","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1000,"y":1856,"z":115,"gx":1856,"gy":-1000,"gz":115,"title_zh":"青蛙地藏","title_en":"Frog Guardian","place_zh":"卡卡利科村","place_en":"Kakariko Village","transcript_zh":"道祖神。青蛙自古以来就象征着好运，也是希卡族信仰的对象。我也双手合十向它祈祷，愿海拉鲁尽早恢复如初，迈向繁荣。","transcript_en":"This frog statue is the guardian of travelers, though I don't believe anyone knows why it's a frog, specifically... It is fascinating that a group as technologically advanced as the Sheikah would still believe in such symbols of good fortune. Maybe it somehow relates to when the Sheikah splintered after a disagreement regarding the royal family... A symbol of hope to one day reunite, perhaps?"},{"seq":168,"id":"vm_zelda_133","no":"No.133","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1017,"y":1873,"z":117,"gx":1873,"gy":-1017,"gz":117,"title_zh":"美洛的梅花园","title_en":"Mellie's Plum Garden","place_zh":"梅莉的梅花园","place_en":"Mellie's Plum Garden","transcript_zh":"梅花园。100年前，英帕为喜得贵子的朋友种下了一棵梅花树作为贺礼。如今已经长得如此高大……看来一直在受人精心照料。照看梅花园的美洛女士，该不会就是当初的……","transcript_en":"A garden for growing plums. A hundred years ago, Impa planted a plum tree here to celebrate a child's birth. It really has grown into something beautiful since that time; the care Mellie has put into maintaining this place is clear to see. Now that I think of it, could she be..."},{"seq":169,"id":"vm_zelda_134","no":"No.134","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":955,"y":1868,"z":123,"gx":1868,"gy":-955,"gz":123,"title_zh":"珂珂娜的花环","title_en":"Koko's Garland","place_zh":"卡卡利科村","place_en":"Kakariko Village","transcript_zh":"小珂珂娜的家。她以前总会给我摘好多好多的花，并和我一起编花环。看着她那么努力，还说要教给妹妹小普莉珂，我不由得回想起小时候母后教我编花环的那段时光。一开始我好像还因为编不好而经常掉眼泪呢……","transcript_en":"The house where Koko lives... She picked such an abundance of flowers for me that we decided to make garlands with them. She said she would teach her little sister, Cottla, how to make them as well. Seeing her work so hard stirred memories of when Mother taught me how to weave garlands together. Though...I found it very difficult at first and may have even cried in frustration..."},{"seq":170,"id":"vm_zelda_135","no":"No.135","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":891,"y":1927,"z":165,"gx":1927,"gy":-891,"gz":165,"title_zh":"可秋拉的内心纠葛","title_en":"Cotera's Considerations","place_zh":"东部高台的深穴","place_en":"East Hill Chasm","transcript_zh":"大妖精可秋拉大人似乎已经不在这里了。可能还是得向她供奉香火钱才行……自从村民们出于好心供奉蔬菜开始，大妖精的力量就肉眼可见地逐渐衰弱了……可秋拉大人想必也是不想枉费村民的一片心意，所以从未说出口吧","transcript_en":"It seems the Great Fairy Cotera no longer lives here. I have heard that the only truly appropriate offering to her was rupees, and after the villagers started offering vegetables, thinking that would suffice, Cotera quickly grew weak. She was too considerate of the villagers' feelings to say anything though..."},{"seq":171,"id":"vm_zelda_136","no":"No.136","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1340,"y":3936,"z":467,"gx":3936,"gy":-1340,"gz":467,"title_zh":"智慧之泉","title_en":"Spring of Wisdom","place_zh":"智慧之泉","place_en":"Spring of Wisdom","transcript_zh":"当年我的封印之力仍未觉醒，下山后迎面而来的便是灾厄复活的绝望噩耗……如果……没有各位英杰和林克坚持不懈带来的希望之光，恐怕就没有今天了……这一次，该轮到我为大家倾尽全力了","transcript_en":"This is the spring where Nayru, Goddess of Wisdom, is worshipped. \"Those younger than 17 lack wisdom and are forbidden from entering the mountain.\" Hm. Today, all I can do is look up at it, but tomorrow, I climb Mount Lanayru. If my sealing power doesn't awaken... No...it will. I'm certain it will be fine."},{"seq":172,"id":"vm_zelda_137","no":"No.137","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2142,"y":3281,"z":102,"gx":3281,"gy":-2142,"gz":102,"title_zh":"家一般的港湾","title_en":"Feeling Truly at Home","place_zh":"哈特诺村","place_en":"Hateno Village","transcript_zh":"哈特诺村。这里是我心目中的第二个家。翻松的泥土和刚割的青草散发清香，拉聂尔山吹来的和风抚摸脸颊……孩子们在村里嬉戏喧闹……看到人们的生活日渐安宁，我深感欣慰。","transcript_en":"I always feel at home when I am in Hateno Village. The smells of well-tended soil and freshly cut grass... The refreshing breeze coming off Mount Lanayru washing over me... The sound of children at play in the village... I am so glad to see life slowly returning to normal here."},{"seq":173,"id":"vm_zelda_138","no":"No.138","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2130,"y":3356,"z":121,"gx":3356,"gy":-2130,"gz":121,"title_zh":"传闻中的时尚追求者","title_en":"The Rumored Fashionista","place_zh":"东风服饰店","place_en":"Ventest Clothing Boutique","transcript_zh":"人们现在有闲心追求时尚，这就是海拉鲁正在逐渐恢复和平的最好证明。想必服饰店的萨格诺小姐就是时尚潮流的发起者。听说蘑菇图案是她在造访阿卡莱地区的一始村时灵光一闪的设计。","transcript_en":"That people have time to consider and enjoy fashion is a sure sign that life is returning to normal in Hyrule. I'm sure much of the credit for the interest in fashion is thanks to Cece's determination and inspiration. I hear the idea for the mushroom pattern came to her when she visited Tarrey Town in Akkala."},{"seq":174,"id":"vm_zelda_139","no":"No.139","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2141,"y":3401,"z":121,"gx":3401,"gy":-2141,"gz":121,"title_zh":"巧匠的灵感","title_en":"Splash of Inspiration","place_zh":"染坊","place_en":"Kochi Dye Shop","transcript_zh":"经营哈特诺染的珂奇屋。店主瑟吉先生在炉子前埋头研究着什么，连标志性的红发都熏得漆黑。听说他儿子瑟法罗的涂鸦带给了他新生意的灵感。真好奇他会弄出什么新花样来。","transcript_en":"Kochi Dye Shop, here in Hateno Village, specializes in dyes. The owner, Sayge, stuck his own head into his dyeing machine and turned his trademark red hair black. Apparently, it happened while he was working on an idea he got from some drawings his son, Sefaro, made. I must admit I am intrigued with what he's up to."},{"seq":175,"id":"vm_zelda_140","no":"No.140","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":1989,"y":3367,"z":128,"gx":3367,"gy":-1989,"gz":128,"title_zh":"希望之光","title_en":"Beacon of Hope","place_zh":"哈特诺学校","place_en":"Hateno School","transcript_zh":"哈特诺学校。我所追求的复兴，是孩子们拥有种种选择的未来。希望这里能够成为新时代的希望之光","transcript_en":"I pray that, as the restoration work continues, Hateno School will become a place where children can find many paths toward their futures—that it will shine as a beacon of hope for generations to come."},{"seq":176,"id":"vm_zelda_141","no":"No.141","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2090,"y":3620,"z":177,"gx":3620,"gy":-2090,"gz":177,"title_zh":"难以忘怀的味道","title_en":"Unforgettable Flavor","place_zh":"哈特诺牧场","place_en":"Hateno Pasture","transcript_zh":"哈特诺牧场。100年前，我承蒙牧场的创办人招待，尝到了至今难忘的美味，可我再次前去造访时，却发现没人知道我说的食物……难道当时的食谱已经失传了吗","transcript_en":"The founder of Hateno Pasture let me try a sample of food that was processed using milk. The subtle texture and mild flavor were so enjoyable that I couldn't stop myself from eating quite a bit of it. I asked to see the recipe, but unfortunately the handwriting was scrawled in such a way that I couldn't make out a single word..."},{"seq":177,"id":"vm_zelda_142","no":"No.142","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2111,"y":3779,"z":250,"gx":3779,"gy":-2111,"gz":250,"title_zh":"往日如烟……","title_en":"In a Puff of Smoke...","place_zh":"哈特诺古代研究所","place_en":"Hateno Ancient Tech Lab","transcript_zh":"哈特诺古代研究所。讨伐灾厄后，所有古代遗物都如尘埃般消失了。这里的每一件东西都是仿真的复制品，但现在已经成为了让后世了解海拉鲁历史的宝贵藏品。","transcript_en":"It seems that when the Calamity was defeated, all of the ancient relics here at the Hateno Ancient Tech Lab turned to dust and disappeared. All that remains are replicas of the originals, and with those gone, these are even more valuable. They will doubtlessly help tell future generations of the history of Hyrule."},{"seq":178,"id":"vm_zelda_143","no":"No.143","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2127,"y":3784,"z":272,"gx":3784,"gy":-2127,"gz":272,"title_zh":"抗衰老的秘密","title_en":"Anti-Aging Secrets","place_zh":"普尔亚的房间","place_en":"Purah's Room","transcript_zh":"普尔亚的房间。黑板上写满了返老还童计划的构想。没想到她是从羊脂中得到启发……不过，她好像已经用腻了小孩子的形象……这三分钟热度的性格和100年前一模一样。","transcript_en":"Purah has used the blackboard in her room to write out the details of how she reversed her physical age. I still can't believe she got the idea from sheep's fat... Regardless, it seems she quickly got bored of her childhood form... It is amusing that, despite a hundred years passing and Purah growing old, then young, then a little older, she hasn't changed in at least one way: she will become obsessive about something yet grow tired of it quickly."},{"seq":179,"id":"vm_zelda_144","no":"No.144","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2448,"y":3912,"z":3,"gx":3912,"gy":-2448,"gz":3,"title_zh":"哈特诺海滩","title_en":"Hateno Beach","place_zh":"哈特诺海滩","place_en":"Hateno Beach","transcript_zh":"放眼望去的景色和100年前别无二致尽管其他地方沧海桑田，这里却一成不变。这个地方像是在告诉我，我大可不必强行做出改变。","transcript_en":"The view from here is, as ever, unchanging. This place is one of the few I know that remains constant. Am I weak for feeling relief at that?"},{"seq":180,"id":"vm_zelda_145","no":"No.145","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2199,"y":3294,"z":112,"gx":3294,"gy":-2199,"gz":112,"title_zh":"天罚","title_en":"Divine Punishment","place_zh":"塔尔荷池塘","place_en":"Firly Pond","transcript_zh":"恶魔像。它突然开口说话，自称为司掌生命与力量之神。一股让我浑身发软的感觉涌上心头，就在我快要失去意识的那一刻，一道闪电劈中恶魔像，令它滚落到了水池之中……我总觉得……这东西定不是什么善物，所以就让他继续沉在水中吧","transcript_en":"A strange horned statue... It suddenly spoke to me, calling itself a dealer in life and power, and I felt an overwhelming sensation, like my life was being drained away. But just as suddenly, a bolt of lightning struck the statue, toppling it into the water... That feeling... I do not think the statue had good intentions. It is best left submerged."},{"seq":181,"id":"vm_zelda_146","no":"No.146","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2301,"y":3302,"z":112,"gx":3302,"gy":-2301,"gz":112,"title_zh":"秘密基地","title_en":"Secret Hideout","place_zh":"塞尔达的家的井","place_en":"Zelda's Secret Well","transcript_zh":"我在挖井的过程中找到了一个隐藏房间。以前可能是和主屋相通的，但历经漫长岁月，想必早已被人们遗忘了吧……腐朽的部分稍加修整过后完全可以继续使用。石制宝箱里面肯定装过非常贵重的东西我也往里面放点什么吧。","transcript_en":"While we were digging a well, I came upon a hidden room. It may have been connected to the main building at one time, but it seems it was forgotten as years passed... Still, it could be used again—with a little work on the more decayed areas. Hmm. I imagine something precious was once stored in that treasure chest... What could I put there?"},{"seq":182,"id":"vm_zelda_147","no":"No.147","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":2288,"y":3317,"z":130,"gx":3317,"gy":-2288,"gz":130,"title_zh":"塞尔达的家","title_en":"Zelda's Home","place_zh":"塞尔达公主的家","place_en":"Princess Zelda's House","transcript_zh":"屋子里有些冷清，所以我把旅途中所见的海拉鲁人文风景的图画挂了起来。除此之外还有……和最最重要的同伴们的回忆","transcript_en":"This room feels a little lonely, so I've decided to decorate it with pictures of the people and places I encountered on my travels. And also...with the memories of my dearest friends..."},{"seq":183,"id":"vm_zelda_148","no":"No.148","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-1897,"y":880,"z":175,"gx":880,"gy":1897,"gz":175,"title_zh":"德库树森林","title_en":"Forest of the Deku Tree","place_zh":"迷途森林","place_en":"Lost Woods","transcript_zh":"迷途森林。穿过这里就能抵达德库树长老所在的森林。还记得我第一次来到这里时，身体都僵住了，母后便让我看看那些树木的表情有多么丰富，接着我就不再感到害怕了。这个地方教会了我改变视角，所看到的世界会变得更加辽阔的道理。","transcript_en":"Once you pass through the Lost Woods, you'll arrive at the forest where the Great Deku Tree lives. When I first visited here, I could hardly move from fright, but Mother soothed my fears by pointing out that where I saw scary, twisted trees, she saw interesting, expressive faces. That is when I truly learned the value of appreciating different perspectives."},{"seq":184,"id":"vm_zelda_149","no":"No.149","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2144,"y":430,"z":162,"gx":430,"gy":2144,"gz":162,"title_zh":"剑的守护者","title_en":"A Sword's Protector","place_zh":"克洛格森林","place_en":"Korok Forest","transcript_zh":"德库树长老。我来这里多少次了呢……？第一次造访此地是刚出生不久……德库树长老赐予的樱花蓓蕾在我的头顶绽放了这代表着我是继承女神之力的人……和欢喜的父王相反，母后的表情很是复杂虽然也遇到了不少痛心之事，但如今我由衷地为自己继承了这股力量而感到高兴。","transcript_en":"The Great Deku Tree watches over the sword that seals the darkness. I also view this tree as a mentor, in a sense. When the knight was chosen to wield the darkness-sealing sword, I felt nearly overcome by my feelings. But the Great Deku Tree offered me words of wisdom in that moment, encouraging me not to give up and that I had my own path to follow. Those words provide comfort to me still."},{"seq":185,"id":"vm_zelda_150","no":"No.150","narrator":"zelda","layer":18,"x":-2112,"y":432,"z":144,"gx":432,"gy":2112,"gz":144,"title_zh":"大师之剑","title_en":"Master Sword","place_zh":"克洛格森林","place_en":"Korok Forest","transcript_zh":"当初林克奄一息的时候……如果没有你的声音指引，我今天就无法站在这里虽然后来再也没有听到你的声音，但拯救世界离不开你的功劳。现在请你好好养伤吧。","transcript_en":"When Link was on the brink of death...had it not been for your voice to guide me, I wouldn't be here now. Though I cannot hear your voice anymore, I still offer you my thanks. It is because of you that the world was saved. Please...rest here and heal your wounds..."},{"seq":186,"id":"vm_kohga_001","no":"No.001","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1332,"y":-3437,"z":-780,"gx":-3437,"gy":-1332,"gz":-780,"title_zh":"可盖大人再临！","title_en":"Master Kohga Returns!","place_zh":"依盖队基地的深穴","place_en":"Yiga Clan Hideout Chasm","transcript_zh":"这里……是地狱？终于轮到我遭报应了吗……不对……我好像还活着……原来是这块鼓起的布料替我吸收了坠落的冲击力吗……但是林克那个混蛋！居然趁我不备搞偷袭，太卑鄙了！再让我见到他，我定要狠狠地教训他……话说回来，这里……是什么地方……？难道是古代人曾居住的地底？！","transcript_en":"Is this...the afterlife? The great beyond? My final reckoning? Nah, it still hurts like I'm alive... And I'm alive thanks to this weird inflated cloth! Talk about helpful, unlike that dastardly Link! How dare he foil the secret technique of the leader of the Yiga Clan! Grrrr... Hang on. Maybe I'm in the Depths... That's where a buncha ancient people lived. Maybe?"},{"seq":187,"id":"vm_kohga_002","no":"No.002","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1360,"y":-3402,"z":-780,"gx":-3402,"gy":-1360,"gz":-780,"title_zh":"破魔之根","title_en":"Lightroots","place_zh":"姆马兹罗之根","place_en":"Umamustor Lightroot","transcript_zh":"说起来这里也太暗了吧！这个微微发光的东西就不能再亮一点吗？！这个绿色的像纹章的东西一点反应都没……这东西到底是什么啊？是植物吗？是从地上……？不……是从地底向着地面生长的吗……？？完全搞不明白！","transcript_en":"This place is waaay too dark! Maybe if these dim, glowing things could get brighter...or if this green...crest thingy reacted at all! And what even is this—some kind of massive plant? It goes so far up... Does it reach all the way from here to the surface?!"},{"seq":188,"id":"vm_kohga_003","no":"No.003","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1321,"y":-3360,"z":-779,"gx":-3360,"gy":-1321,"gz":-779,"title_zh":"游荡的魄","title_en":"Wandering Poes","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"哦哦！稍稍晃了一下！每次想要触碰它，我的背后就一股凉意。这难道是人类的魂魄……如果没错……那这里果真是……地地地……地狱？！","transcript_en":"Hoho! It shook a little there! But touching it also sent a shiver down MY spine. Huh... Maybe they're...spirits? But if they are, then th-that means this IS the afterlife!"},{"seq":189,"id":"vm_kohga_004","no":"No.004","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1521,"y":-2934,"z":-920,"gx":-2934,"gy":-1521,"gz":-920,"title_zh":"敏锐的第六感","title_en":"A Keen Sixth Sense","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"哦……有泛着绿光的东西在飘……那是什么……？我……看看……这是……小瓶子？？里面好像有东西……但是拿不出来……算了，虽然搞不懂这是什么，但我的第六感已经有了答案！这绝对是好东西！姑且带走吧~","transcript_en":"What's this floating green thing? Hrm...huff... This some kinda bottle? What's inside? I'll just... JUST... Fine! Don't open! I'm still gonna hang on to you. My sixth sense says you're important."},{"seq":190,"id":"vm_kohga_005","no":"No.005","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1680,"y":-2557,"z":-869,"gx":-2557,"gy":-1680,"gz":-869,"title_zh":"可盖大人的收获①","title_en":"Master Kohga's Education, Part 1","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"这是古代人曾使用的……机关？嗯？这个尖尖的圆筒是什么……感觉可以让它立起来……我来试试……当椅子坐也太晃了！这破玩意儿，看我把你砸个稀巴烂！怎么回事？怎么开始发光了……?","transcript_en":"Hrm. This some kinda ancient doodad? It's flat there and pointed here... Huuup... Aah, my butt! Ow, what a terrible seat. Oh, take this, terrible seat. Ha! Gah! ...Wh-what? Why are you glowing?"},{"seq":191,"id":"vm_kohga_006","no":"No.006","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1916,"y":-2915,"z":-732,"gx":-2915,"gy":-1916,"gz":-732,"title_zh":"可盖大人的收获②","title_en":"Master Kohga's Education, Part 2","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"又是堆放机关的地方……刚才那个圆筒状的东西突然飞出去，搞得我那么狼犯……不过那东西随处可见，或许它是古代人的移动方式吧……那么这圆滚滚的东西说不定也会浮起来吧！接着敲敲看这玩意吧！","transcript_en":"Aha, more ancient doodads! Lots like the last one too... Crazy thing firing off into the air scared the bananas outta me. Huh... I bet the ancients used them to get around! Which means...I can too! C'mere, round thingy! Time to show Master Kohga what you can do. Hee-yah!"},{"seq":192,"id":"vm_kohga_007","no":"No.007","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2362,"y":-2701,"z":-516,"gx":-2701,"gy":-2362,"gz":-516,"title_zh":"烟雾蘑菇","title_en":"Puffshroom","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"地上从没见过这种蘑菇……我来尝一口……呜咳咳……这股烟是什么！我看不见了……！看来这不是什么食物，而是扰乱视线的手段……以防之后遭到怪物袭击，就塞几个在身上","transcript_en":"Ooo, this is a new mushroom! I've never seen anything like it on the surface... Maybe just one little bite. Ack! What is this smoke?! I can't see anything... Oh, just like a smoke screen! I should hang on to a few of these for the next time things are looking dicey..."},{"seq":193,"id":"vm_kohga_008","no":"No.008","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2381,"y":-2989,"z":-477,"gx":-2989,"gy":-2381,"gz":-477,"title_zh":"邀请加入依盖队","title_en":"Invitation to Join the Yiga Clan","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠地底","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Depths","transcript_zh":"哎哟……原来地底也有波克布林啊……曾经效忠于魔王大人的忠诚仆人，我本想拉它们入伙，可这些家伙只因为我是人就袭击我，太不像话了……不过，这里的家伙们会使用工具采集物品，似乎有一定的智力……或许能和它们谈谈？","transcript_en":"OK, so there are Bokoblins down here... And they're smart enough to mine for...something...using tools... But they attack me right away. Here I thought faithful servants of the Magnificent One would want to be friends... Could have at least talked first..."},{"seq":194,"id":"vm_kohga_009","no":"No.009","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2511,"y":-3290,"z":-475,"gx":-3290,"gy":-2511,"gz":-475,"title_zh":"和波克布林决裂","title_en":"Escaping the Bokoblins","place_zh":"塔塔亚马之根","place_en":"Tatayam Lightroot","transcript_zh":"终于甩掉那些波克布林了……那些家伙似乎无法靠近这个光源……亏我还想任命它们为依盖队地底部队呢。竟然不分敌我就攻击……唉，队员们现在都还好吗……我好想你们阳","transcript_en":"Heh, good riddance to those Bokoblins... I guess they don't like this light. I was going to let them join my new Yiga Clan Depths Squad, but they definitely like attacking me too much. Makes me miss the Yiga Clan. I wonder what they're up to..."},{"seq":195,"id":"vm_kohga_010","no":"No.010","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2511,"y":-3196,"z":-475,"gx":-3196,"gy":-2511,"gz":-475,"title_zh":"卡拉卡拉废矿","title_en":"Abandoned Kara Kara Mine","place_zh":"卡拉卡拉废矿","place_en":"Abandoned Kara Kara Mine","transcript_zh":"这是什么地方？炉子里还燃着火焰，或许刚刚还有人用过吧？我刚才在远处看见，有颗头从这块绿色的东西里伸了出来，晃来晃去……是我太饿产生幻觉了吗","transcript_en":"What's the deal with this place? The furnace is blazing away but no one to be seen... Though from a distance, it did look like this green thing was moving! Hm. Maybe I should go find something to eat. Things will go bad if I start hallucinating."},{"seq":196,"id":"vm_kohga_011","no":"No.011","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2719,"y":-3205,"z":-481,"gx":-3205,"gy":-2719,"gz":-481,"title_zh":"混乱花的诱惑","title_en":"Tempted by the Muddle Bud","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠地底","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Depths","transcript_zh":"呜哇！就是它吗？这就是那股腐烂恶臭的源头吗？！太臭了！……臭……但莫名地……感觉……上瘾……我……头好晕……嗯？那边在进行开采的人……不是队员们吗？可刚才我还以为那是一群波克布林，不多想了！喂～大伙～","transcript_en":"Ah-ha! Is THIS the source of that horrible, rotting smell? It. Is. AWFUL. I can't stand it. I hate it! I...don't want to stop smelling it. Whoa. Little bit dizzy all of a... Hey, over there! Those aren't Bokoblins—they're Yiga! Guys! GUUUYS!"},{"seq":197,"id":"vm_kohga_012","no":"No.012","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2844,"y":-3216,"z":-472,"gx":-3216,"gy":-2844,"gz":-472,"title_zh":"伫立的人影","title_en":"Standing Shadows","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠地底","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Depths","transcript_zh":"救、救命啊！我遭到了波克布林的追杀……嗯？可我确实看见这有人影的……是我看错了吗？我刚刚还把怪物错当成了队员……孤独的感觉原来这么煎熬啊……现在哪怕是遇到林克……不行，我绝饶不了他……我沦落至此，都是他的错！","transcript_en":"Is that... At last! Someone to help me! There are Bokoblins chasing... Huh? Coulda sworn there was someone here... Grrr! No one tells you how lonely solitude is... I'd even accept the company of that Link character... NO! What am I saying? I'll never forgive him for casting me down into the Depths! Never!"},{"seq":198,"id":"vm_kohga_013","no":"No.013","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3033,"y":-3214,"z":-471,"gx":-3214,"gy":-3033,"gz":-471,"title_zh":"在外靠朋友","title_en":"Silent Companions","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠地底","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Depths","transcript_zh":"我还以为这次总该是人了……结果是个石像……算了，早就料想到会是这种结果……不过仔细一瞧，这一带到处都是石像啊？反正我也不知道该往哪里走，就去姑娘们凝视的方向看看","transcript_en":"Ugh, I was SURE this one was a person. But nope, just another statue. Figures... Hey, there are a lot of statues down here. Maybe I'll just head from one to the next, starting with where this one is looking. I haven't got anywhere else to be..."},{"seq":199,"id":"vm_kohga_014","no":"No.014","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2909,"y":-3838,"z":-487,"gx":-3838,"gy":-2909,"gz":-487,"title_zh":"香蕉的记忆","title_en":"Essence of Banana","place_zh":"格鲁德废矿","place_en":"Abandoned Gerudo Mine","transcript_zh":"又是废墟啊……我还以为至少能见到个村庄呢……水也早就喝完了……甚至还仿佛听到了队员们呼唤我的声音……看来我气数将尽……回想我继承可盖之名的日子，还像是昨天一样……嗯？这股香味……这、这是我最爱的采摘后放置五日熟成的香蕉！大……大伙！真的是你们吗？！","transcript_en":"Oh good, more ruins. Couldn't be an actual village, could it? Hrmph, and no water either. I keep hallucinating Yiga calling out to me. \"Kohga... Kohga...\" Feels like yesterday that I inherited that name... So long ago—that smell! That's...banana, set out to ripen for five days! JUST HOW I LIKE IT. It must be them! Yiga Clan! GUYS?!"},{"seq":200,"id":"vm_kohga_015","no":"No.015","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3456,"y":-3760,"z":-469,"gx":-3760,"gy":-3456,"gz":-469,"title_zh":"可盖大人的收获③","title_en":"Master Kohga's Education, Part 3","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠地底","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Depths","transcript_zh":"为了建立依盖队的地底支部，我命令队员们往地底筹集香蕉……不对，是物资……在此期间我得弄明白这个机关……这块圆滚滚的布……如果在这个凹陷处点火……噢噢，鼓起来了……喂喂喂，别飞了！停下！给我回来！","transcript_en":"The Yiga are gathering critical bananas—I mean supplies—for us to set up the Depths branch of the Yiga Clan. While they do that, I need to figure out how this device works. Cloth with a hole at the bottom... What if I put fire here? Hmm... Uh huh... Oh! Oh, no! S-stop! Don't fly away!"},{"seq":201,"id":"vm_kohga_016","no":"No.016","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3739,"y":-4088,"z":-466,"gx":-4088,"gy":-3739,"gz":-466,"title_zh":"藏匿在墓地中的秘密","title_en":"The Cemetery's Secret","place_zh":"格鲁德地下坟场","place_en":"Gerudo Underground Cemetery","transcript_zh":"这里是墓地？可里面连一根骨头都没有啊……哼哼，墓地只是障眼法其中一定藏着什么特别的东西……这个宝箱……啧，完全锈掉了，打不开啊……其他的……这是笔记……吗？虽然我不认识这些字……这……这是……！呵呵呵……看来上天还没有抛弃我。","transcript_en":"Is this some kinda grave... Hmm... No bones though. Not a grave after all, are you? I bet you're hiding something... Aha! A treasure chest, ha ha! Now I'll just...open... Grr! Rusted! Anything else here? Ah, a notebook! I can't read the letters, but...... Hehehe, I know what this is! It seems luck hasn't abandoned me yet!"},{"seq":202,"id":"vm_kohga_017","no":"No.017","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3723,"y":-4308,"z":-480,"gx":-4308,"gy":-3723,"gz":-480,"title_zh":"蛮暴之徒聚集的地方","title_en":"Unsafe Gathering","place_zh":"沙漠竞技场","place_en":"Desert Coliseum","transcript_zh":"那个宝箱……是陷阱……我光靠感觉就能分辨出来。只要像这样靠近看吧，被关起来了！啊哈哈，没说错吧！可别小瞧我啊！啊……喂……等等！我并不想和你们打","transcript_en":"Nuh-uh, hehehe! You can't fool me! This place has all the makings of a trap. See, if I get closer, like this... There! Trap sprung! Haha! So easy to— Hey, what are you— S-stop it! I don't wanna fight you!"},{"seq":203,"id":"vm_kohga_018","no":"No.018","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3676,"y":-4493,"z":-477,"gx":-4493,"gy":-3676,"gz":-477,"title_zh":"地底的大化石","title_en":"Great Skeletons of the Depths","place_zh":"格鲁德暗化石","place_en":"Gerudo Dark Skeleton","transcript_zh":"哦哦～以前在格鲁德沙漠也看到过这种骨头，没想到地底也有这种庞然大物……慢着……地上和地底是相通的……难道说……曾经生活在地上的生物借助深穴移居到了地底？","transcript_en":"Whoooa. I've seen some big skeletons in Gerudo Desert, but I don't think I've run into anything like that down here... Hm. Hmmmmmm. If the surface and the Depths are connected, then that means the creatures living up above could come down here! I think!"},{"seq":204,"id":"vm_kohga_019","no":"No.019","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3411,"y":-4482,"z":-478,"gx":-4482,"gy":-3411,"gz":-478,"title_zh":"可盖大人的收获④","title_en":"Master Kohga's Education, Part 4","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠地底","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Depths","transcript_zh":"根据在墓地捡到的笔记中描绘的内容，这些机关似乎要相互拼接在一起使用……把立足处……牢牢捆在这个布做的零件上……然后把这个会出风的东西装在这里……好了。接下来只要点火就完成了。我还想仔细调查一下笔记的内容……暂且先回到基地的洞穴下方吧。","transcript_en":"The pictures in that book from the graveyard were very, very clear. These things all attach in different ways to make something else! So if I this cloth...connect it to the platform...put this wind-blowing thing here... Ha! Then if I lit a fire under it, It'd work! Hehehe... Yeah, I need to study this notebook. Time to head to the hole under the hideout!"},{"seq":205,"id":"vm_kohga_020","no":"No.020","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1564,"y":-3112,"z":-913,"gx":-3112,"gy":-1564,"gz":-913,"title_zh":"崛起！依盖队帝国！","title_en":"Building Up the Yiga Clan Empire","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"我的使命才刚刚开始。首先要在这片距离基地不远的地方建立据点……但我还是很在意那本在墓地捡到的笔记。里面画的应该是设计图……每一样设计都十分天马行空……不过如果这些都能成为现实的话……或许我该再深入调查一下地底","transcript_en":"Hehehe... OK, so I think it'll work to set up a base here, close to the hideout... But what do I do about that graveyard notebook? The drawings in it are ab-so-lutely schematics of some kind...but they look like impossible, unbuildable wastes of time... BUT! If they aren't... I should explore the Depths some more..."},{"seq":206,"id":"vm_kohga_021","no":"No.021","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1299,"y":-4616,"z":-941,"gx":-4616,"gy":-1299,"gz":-941,"title_zh":"贪吃的巨霸迦马","title_en":"The Glutton Frox","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"那只巨大的怪物是什么玩意啊！！多亏了我藏在怀里的炸弹花，不然我就要被一口吞掉了！我还以为那是品质不错的矿石呢，居然敢骗我！可恶的大胖蛤蟆！","transcript_en":"Yooou big, stupid toad thing! Why do you have good-looking ore on your head if you're just gonna try and eat me when I check it out?! I hope you like that bomb flower I gave you! I hope it gives you gas!"},{"seq":207,"id":"vm_kohga_022","no":"No.022","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":979,"y":-4039,"z":-1110,"gx":-4039,"gy":-979,"gz":-1110,"title_zh":"古代的守卫者","title_en":"An Ancient Guard","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"这家伙……我记得笔记里……啊啊，找到了！就是这个！虽然我不认字，但图片不管在哪个时代都没什么区别。我看看……只要靠近这东西就会化作人形……大概是守卫吧。从古至今，靠近闪着红光的东西总没好事。还是小心为妙，小心为妙哦。","transcript_en":"The notebook had info about this thing, I'm sure. What page was that? Ummm...ummm... Aha! Here we go. According to these pictures, this creature gets all...person shaped when you get too close. Must be some kind of guard? It's got glowing red eyes, and those are ALWAYS bad news. I'll...keep my distance."},{"seq":208,"id":"vm_kohga_023","no":"No.023","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-1794,"y":-1982,"z":-364,"gx":-1982,"gy":1794,"gz":-364,"title_zh":"命名为左纳乌装置！","title_en":"They Shall Be Called Zonai Devices!","place_zh":"海拉鲁丘陵地底","place_en":"Hyrule Ridge Depths","transcript_zh":"我捡到的笔记恐怕是左纳乌人的东西……如果我读得没错的话……这字应该是左……纳……乌……而这边的是装……置吧……算了，管它对不对呢，从今天起它就叫左纳乌装置啦！","transcript_en":"I bet the notebook I found belonged to a Zonai. And if I'm right about that, then...this shape must be \"zo,\" and I think this one is \"na,\" and THIS is \"i.\" Hmmm... \"De...vice...\" \"Zonai device...\" Zonai device! Yeah, that seems right, and I don't care if it isn't!"},{"seq":209,"id":"vm_kohga_024","no":"No.024","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-1841,"y":-2419,"z":-716,"gx":-2419,"gy":1841,"gz":-716,"title_zh":"通天输送带","title_en":"A Way Up","place_zh":"塔邦挞边境地底","place_en":"Tabantha Frontier Depths","transcript_zh":"这玩意儿应该是往地上运输东西的装置……但头顶上并没有洞，应该运不上去吧！从笔记上的图案来看，东西会被一下子传送到上面……啊—搞不懂！完全搞不懂！我还想利用它跟地面基地相互输送物资呢，看来是行不通了。","transcript_en":"So... Obviously this was meant to send things to the surface. What I don't understand is how it moves things through the ground. The pictures in the notebook look like it just...happens. They just...go through. Grrr... I don't get it! And I can't use this to send stuff to a base on the surface if I can't figure it out!"},{"seq":210,"id":"vm_kohga_025","no":"No.025","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-2692,"y":-1029,"z":-273,"gx":-1029,"gy":2692,"gz":-273,"title_zh":"变成石头的巨人","title_en":"A Stone Giant","place_zh":"断崖魔人像","place_en":"Cliff Bargainer Statue","transcript_zh":"呼……这里是脸……这么大个东西居然没被记载在笔记里……难道它不是左纳乌人造的吗……是做了什么坏事被女神变成了石头？女神眼中的恶即是我眼中的正义。老兄你如果生在我这个时代，我们也许会是对好搭档哦。","transcript_en":"Annnd there's the face. Hm. You're not in the notebook. Does that mean the Zonai didn't make you? And how'd you get turned to stone, anyway? Maybe the Goddess did it because you did something bad... Well, bad by her standards. And if she didn't like you, I bet we woulda gotten along."},{"seq":211,"id":"vm_kohga_026","no":"No.026","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-3123,"y":319,"z":-621,"gx":319,"gy":3123,"gz":-621,"title_zh":"古栗欧克的巢","title_en":"Gleeok Den","place_zh":"古栗欧克的巢","place_en":"Gleeok Den","transcript_zh":"呵呵……地面已经整平了，四周还被崖壁包围，太适合建造据点了！但这些石像不符合我的审美……干脆拆了，然后打造一个我的石像吧。造型大概是这种感觉……不，再这样些……嗯？这嘶吼声是什么……呀一！那是什么怪物！这、这里难道是那家伙的巢穴吗？撤撤撤……撤退","transcript_en":"Ho ho ho! Look at this level ground! And cliffs on all sides... This would be the perfect spot for a base! I...would have to get rid of those statues though. Oh! And replace them with statues of me! But...what poses would be best? Maybe...THIS! Or I could do...HA! What about—wait. Is that growling? Ah! What is THAT?! AAH!"},{"seq":212,"id":"vm_kohga_027","no":"No.027","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-2873,"y":714,"z":-660,"gx":714,"gy":2873,"gz":-660,"title_zh":"可盖大人的收获⑤","title_en":"Master Kohga's Education, Part 5","place_zh":"奥尔汀山脉地底","place_en":"Eldin Mountains Depths","transcript_zh":"哦哦！找到了！我要找的就是这个像操纵杆的左纳乌装置！只要有了它，队员们应该就不需要特地练习，也能操作左纳乌装置了！那就让我来试试制造笔记里那个像鸟一样的交通工具吧。","transcript_en":"Whoa, yes! There we go! Finally, a stick-shaped Zonai device that looks like it could steer things! Like a...steering stick! With this, the Yiga Clan will be able to use Zonai Devices with only a little bit of training! Plus, now I can try making this bird-like thing from the notebook..."},{"seq":213,"id":"vm_kohga_028","no":"No.028","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-2829,"y":1164,"z":-754,"gx":1164,"gy":2829,"gz":-754,"title_zh":"死亡之山的洗礼","title_en":"Death Mountain Initiation","place_zh":"火之神殿","place_en":"Fire Temple","transcript_zh":"听……呜……不行，太热了，我受不了了！这里难道是死亡之山的正下方吗？我现在身上也没有防火药，感觉附近也找不到耐火蜥蜴……眼下必须先撤退！掉头掉头～！","transcript_en":"Just beyond the Maw of Death Mountain is a scorching region. The heat from the flow of lava can be intense—so intense, in fact, that it can take one's life should they fail to prepare accordingly. My bodyguards forbade me from going any farther, yet it is my duty to keep a close watch on the Divine Beasts we will be fighting alongside. This mission proves to be exceedingly dangerous..."},{"seq":214,"id":"vm_kohga_029","no":"No.029","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-1849,"y":909,"z":-634,"gx":909,"gy":1849,"gz":-634,"title_zh":"可盖大人的收获⑥","title_en":"Master Kohga's Education, Part 6","place_zh":"海拉鲁大森林地底","place_en":"Great Hyrule Forest Depths","transcript_zh":"终于脱离灼热地狱了……哦哦！有个像车轮的东西！我看看，小的轮子能方便转弯……而大的轮子能应付恶劣路面……配合我们依盖队的运动神经，就算要骑独轮车应该也没问题。","transcript_en":"OK, I think I've finally escaped that scorching misery of a place... Oh! Wheels! Big ones AND small ones! Hmm...I bet the small ones are really maneuverable, but those big ones would be great for tough paths... Oooh, we Yiga have such good reflexes and balance, I bet we could even make a unicycle with these!"},{"seq":215,"id":"vm_kohga_030","no":"No.030","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-1407,"y":1021,"z":-543,"gx":1021,"gy":1407,"gz":-543,"title_zh":"暗萤火虫","title_en":"A Deep Firefly","place_zh":"齐洛利树海","place_en":"Minshi Grove","transcript_zh":"那……那个发光的生物是什么！是虫……虫子？也就是说，如果把它们做成药，就能解决这伸手不见五指的问题了……偷偷摸摸……唉……要是有依盖队的服装，偷偷靠近虫子这种事简直易如反掌……真的假的啊？！我可从没听说过这种事……树居然会动啊！","transcript_en":"OK, what is that glowing creature? Some kinda...bug. Maybe we could use it in an elixir that helps with the darkness down here... Gotta catch it first, but that'll be easy! Nothing is sneakier than a Yiga in their Yiga Clan clothes... Uuuh, what? Are you kidding me? Is that tree WALKING?!"},{"seq":216,"id":"vm_kohga_031","no":"No.031","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-354,"y":2221,"z":-505,"gx":2221,"gy":354,"gz":-505,"title_zh":"卓拉的石像","title_en":"Zora Statues","place_zh":"拉聂尔湿地地底","place_en":"Lanayru Wetlands Depths","transcript_zh":"这个石像的形状看着像是卓拉族那么那座女人像可能就是格鲁德族？既然如此……继续跟着石像指引前进，应该能找到什么人造物吧。但如果真是这样……这片地区的上方难道是拉聂尔地区？地底的空间或许和地上一样大……难怪我调查了那么久，都看不到尽头……","transcript_en":"This statue looks a lot like a Zora... Which means that statue of a woman I saw before was probably a Gerudo. And if I follow this statue, I'll probably find something man-made eventually too... I think I'm beneath the Lanayru region, but that'd mean the Depths are massive! I'll never finish exploring them..."},{"seq":217,"id":"vm_kohga_032","no":"No.032","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-569,"y":3300,"z":-750,"gx":3300,"gy":569,"gz":-750,"title_zh":"拉聂尔废矿","title_en":"Abandoned Lanayru Mine","place_zh":"拉聂尔废矿","place_en":"Abandoned Lanayru Mine","transcript_zh":"之前卓拉族石像所指的位置就是这里吧……格鲁德族雕像指向的也是类似的地方，似乎是个非常重要的设施。这四周看起来很牢固，我们就充分发挥地理优势，把这里当作依盖帝国的据点吧！","transcript_en":"So this is where all those Zora statues were leading me to... kinda like how the Gerudo statues pointed the way. Must be important! And sturdy, by the look of it. A perfect place for a Yiga Clan base!"},{"seq":218,"id":"vm_kohga_033","no":"No.033","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1193,"y":1815,"z":-629,"gx":1815,"gy":-1193,"gz":-629,"title_zh":"废矿的居民","title_en":"What Lives in the Abandoned Mine?","place_zh":"卡卡利科废矿","place_en":"Abandoned Kakariko Mine","transcript_zh":"我亲眼看到了！这家伙果然在动！它一察觉到我就蜷缩起来了！笔记里也记载着它伸出头的样子！没想到神代的造物至今还能运作……先拿回去研究一下吧……咕……咕啊啊啊重……重死了……算了，这家伙就让小的们来调查吧。","transcript_en":"This thing was definitely moving! It withdrew the moment it noticed me, but I saw it! Its neck was all stretched out just like the pictures in the notebook! I can't believe something so ancient still works... Better take it with me. OK lift with your legs and— Oh, wow you're heavy! Never mind! The younger Yiga can haul this home."},{"seq":219,"id":"vm_kohga_034","no":"No.034","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1774,"y":2647,"z":-552,"gx":2647,"gy":-1774,"gz":-552,"title_zh":"溢出的狂放之气","title_en":"Oozing Madness","place_zh":"东哈特尔地底","place_en":"East Necluda Depths","transcript_zh":"我一眼就看出来了！这红红的东西绝对很危险！最近到处都渗出了这种东西。只是稍微碰一下，感觉灵魂就要被吸走了，真是太麻烦了！不过换句话说……不直接触碰到它就没事了。只要有我的“万能疾行机器滑行DEATH1\"在，就没什么好怕的！","transcript_en":"Ho-ho, I knew it the moment I saw it—that red ooze is NOT good. It feels like part of my soul is being stolen right out of me at the slightest touch. And lately the stuff has been getting everywhere. BUT! I figured out the secret: don't touch it! And THAT is why the HOVERDOOM MK. 1 is the best thing ever."},{"seq":220,"id":"vm_kohga_035","no":"No.035","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3214,"y":1402,"z":-597,"gx":1402,"gy":-3214,"gz":-597,"title_zh":"魂之神殿","title_en":"Spirit Temple","place_zh":"魂之神殿","place_en":"Spirit Temple","transcript_zh":"这笔记都快被我翻破页了，不过我也因此基本理解左纳乌文字了。我捡到的这本笔记，是一个叫米湿鲁的家伙写的，似乎是最后一个负责管理这座设施的左纳乌人。笔记中提到这里有正在建造的魔像，来了才发现……这里只有枭的雕像嘛！难道这座石像就是魔像？！","transcript_en":"Turns out if I stare at Zonai letters long enough, I can learn to read them! It also turns out someone named Mineru wrote this notebook I found. They were apparently the last Zonai to manage this place... Anyway, I came here looking for prototype constructs, not a big owl statue. And that isn't a construct! Err...right?"},{"seq":221,"id":"vm_kohga_036","no":"No.036","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2195,"y":867,"z":-559,"gx":867,"gy":-2195,"gz":-559,"title_zh":"魔像制造房","title_en":"Construct Factory","place_zh":"魔像制造房","place_en":"Construct Factory","transcript_zh":"我还以为这里有实验品魔像呢，结果只是个空壳……原本还打算物尽其用的。既然没法用，那只好放弃了。反正我有米涅鲁绘制的魔像设计图，没有成品，那我就自己来造。造一台由我亲自研制的，只属于我自己的魔像！","transcript_en":"All right, so instead of prototype constructs, this place is...empty. That's great. Not like I had plans to use everything I was gonna find... At least I have the schematics for Mineru's construct! I can just make that myself. A construct by me, for me. Heeheeheeheehee..."},{"seq":222,"id":"vm_kohga_037","no":"No.037","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2616,"y":-1259,"z":-516,"gx":-1259,"gy":-2616,"gz":-516,"title_zh":"超极恶爆炎 可盖尔爆诞","title_en":"Mecha Kohga 5000 - Deluxe","place_zh":"格鲁德高地地底","place_en":"Gerudo Highlands Depths","transcript_zh":"我本以为左纳乌装置是用来移动的，居然还有会喷火的龙头，真是危险……慢着……呵呵呵……我想到了……把这个和尖刺组装到我的魔像上，如此一来，实力肯定不俗……就叫它“超极恶爆炎可盖尔”吧！","transcript_en":"So I thought Zonai devices were only good for getting around, but a fire-breathing dragon head? That's really...dangerous... Oh-ho, I have an idea! If I take this and some spikes and add them to my construct... Yes, YES! This could be amazing. This could be incredible! This could be...\"Mecha Kohga 5000 - Deluxe\"!"},{"seq":223,"id":"vm_kohga_038","no":"No.038","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2330,"y":-969,"z":-519,"gx":-969,"gy":-2330,"gz":-519,"title_zh":"不速之客","title_en":"Uninvited Guests","place_zh":"初始台地南边深穴","place_en":"Great Plateau South Chasm","transcript_zh":"据说因为前阵子的地震，不只基地整片海拉鲁大陆都多了不少深穴。我还听说塞尔达组建的调查队已经开始着手调查地底了。真是可恨，明明是我先来的！让我遇见了就统统干掉！不过转念一想……调查的人手越多越好……就先放任他们一阵吧","transcript_en":"So that last earthquake opened up a bunch of holes to the surface, and apparently Zelda has some new minions. They're calling themselves a \"survey team\"—boring—and they have started poking around down here in the Depths. Rude. RUDE! I was here first! I could erase them from existence the moment I see them, but... Maybe I should let them look around and see what they find? THEN erase them! HA!"},{"seq":224,"id":"vm_kohga_039","no":"No.039","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1921,"y":-799,"z":-523,"gx":-799,"gy":-1921,"gz":-523,"title_zh":"中央大废矿","title_en":"Great Abandoned Central Mine","place_zh":"中央大废矿","place_en":"Great Abandoned Central Mine","transcript_zh":"根据墓地捡到的笔记记载……这里的魔像会传授一种左纳乌之力，可以记忆组装过的物品并瞬间制造出来但问题在于那个绿色的认证纹章！我至今进行了各种尝试，它却一点反应都没有……既然如此……剩下的就只能交给小的们研究了！","transcript_en":"Yeah, this is definitely the place the notebook mentioned. It says a construct here will let you use Zonai power to memorize and rebuild a design once it's been made. That would be really useful, except there's another one of those green crests! And it doesn't do anything! Grrr... Someone else can figure it out!"},{"seq":225,"id":"vm_kohga_040","no":"No.040","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1594,"y":-226,"z":-469,"gx":-226,"gy":-1594,"gz":-469,"title_zh":"来自卧底的报告","title_en":"Spy Report","place_zh":"中央海拉鲁地底","place_en":"Central Hyrule Depths","transcript_zh":"据潜入调查队的队员报告，魔王大人居然苏醒了，而且塞尔达和林克都下落不明！真是天大的好消息，天大的好机会！我们身为他的家臣，可得为随时支援那位无上大人做好准备！","transcript_en":"It is a good day! I got a report from one of my spies in the survey team—they say the Demon King has awakened! And both Zelda and Link have gone missing! This is the perfect opportunity to show the Magnificent One that we, his best and most loyal retainers, are ready to support him!"},{"seq":226,"id":"vm_kohga_041","no":"No.041","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1852,"y":-1109,"z":-613,"gx":-1109,"gy":-1852,"gz":-613,"title_zh":"复苏的秘泉","title_en":"Secret Spring of Revival","place_zh":"复苏的秘泉","place_en":"Secret Spring of Revival","transcript_zh":"哈……这温泉太舒服了……我把据点的候选地点和道具的用法都教给小的们了，剩下的事就交给他们吧……准备工作也即将完成……是时候前往见那位无上大人了……唯独这件事是其他人无法代劳的。","transcript_en":"Ahhhh... OK, the Yiga Clan knows where and how to build the base. They can handle the menial work from here. Meanwhile after I'm done soaking—I need to hurry to the Magnificent One. A meeting with him is not something I would leave to anyone else... Ahhh..."},{"seq":227,"id":"vm_kohga_042","no":"No.042","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3323,"y":-2285,"z":-474,"gx":-2285,"gy":-3323,"gz":-474,"title_zh":"左纳乌能源","title_en":"Zonai Charge","place_zh":"格鲁德沙漠地底","place_en":"Gerudo Desert Depths","transcript_zh":"潜入调查队的卧底队员传回了有趣的消息！这里之所以到处都是左纳乌人的痕迹，是因为他们在地底从名为左纳尼乌姆的矿石中抽取能源……有炉子的地方原来都是废弃的矿坑啊那好！这么厉害的能源，我全都要了！","transcript_en":"I heard a reeeally interesting bit of news from one of my spies in the Zonai Survey Team. It seems there's lots of Zonai stuff down here because the ancient Zonai were digging all over the Depths to find an ore called Zonaite. Which must mean the place with the big furnace is an abandoned mine... And THAT obviously means this incredible source of energy was meant for me to control!"},{"seq":228,"id":"vm_kohga_043","no":"No.043","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-1847,"y":-3513,"z":-416,"gx":-3513,"gy":1847,"gz":-416,"title_zh":"海布拉废矿","title_en":"Abandoned Hebra Mine","place_zh":"海布拉废矿","place_en":"Abandoned Hebra Mine","transcript_zh":"利特族的石像在中途不见了，我还觉得奇怪呢，没想到入口居然在地上……位置还偏偏在利特村的正下方……难道其他石像所指向的废矿坑都在亚人村落的下方……？只要从下方进攻，就能打他们一个措手不及……当魔王大人践踏地上之时，就由我们依盖队来扫荡这帮亚人吧！","transcript_en":"It seemed really strange that the Rito statues ended abruptly, but turns out the entrance is on the surface, and it's right under Rito Village. Hmm... Maybe all the mines those statues point to are under big settlements? If that's true, we could employ some sneaky-sneaky stabby-stabby and attack from below while they're distracted. Magnificent One, I hope you approve of my incredibly clever plan!"},{"seq":229,"id":"vm_kohga_044","no":"No.044","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-3531,"y":-892,"z":-682,"gx":-892,"gy":3531,"gz":-682,"title_zh":"洛美遗迹","title_en":"Lomei","place_zh":"北洛美地下层","place_en":"North Lomei Depths Labyrinth","transcript_zh":"嗯嗯嗯……呜……还差一点……唉～进不去……还以为我小巧的脸庞能行，没想到我的香蕉肚被格板卡住了……本想着有方块魔像的地方就会有宝物。算了算了，不找了！肯定又是那种根本打不开的绿色宝箱。","transcript_en":"Grrr...ugh...heee... Almost... Gah! No good. Curse my banana gut! The price I pay for those lovely yellow fruits... Ugh, I just KNOW there's gotta be a great treasure if a Flux Construct is here. But no. Bananas are once again my undoing. I'm done with this. That treasure chest probably won't open anyway!"},{"seq":230,"id":"vm_kohga_045","no":"No.045","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-3709,"y":657,"z":-540,"gx":657,"gy":3709,"gz":-540,"title_zh":"龙行之处","title_en":"The Dragon's Path","place_zh":"奥尔汀山脉地底","place_en":"Eldin Mountains Depths","transcript_zh":"我感觉上面有什么东西在？大概是我的错觉吧……？怎么突然刮大风了……嗯？嗯嗯嗯？那那……那是什么啊？！我看得不太清楚，那个难、难道……是……是龙？大、大伙快看那个……！你说什么？什么都看不见？！再再……再仔细看看啊！","transcript_en":"Huh? What's that? It feels like something is overhead... And the wind... Did it just pick up? But I don't... Oh. OH! What's that?! It's hard to make it out but... Is that a dra...a dra...a dragon? HOW DID I NOT NOTICE A DRAGON?!"},{"seq":231,"id":"vm_kohga_046","no":"No.046","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-3031,"y":4014,"z":-612,"gx":4014,"gy":3031,"gz":-612,"title_zh":"水上部队培训所","title_en":"Yiga Clan: Aquatics Division","place_zh":"深远阿卡莱地底","place_en":"Deep Akkala Depths","transcript_zh":"哦……好大一片湖啊。这里非常适合培训我们依盖队的地底水上部队。必须制造强大的机器，然后掌握操纵技术，尽快提高队员们的熟练度！无论如何都要赶在那位大人复活之前完成！","transcript_en":"Ho...hooo... That is a really big lake. Perfect for the Aquatic Division of the Yiga Clan. We'll have to move quickly to build more powerful water vehicles. And obviously we'll need to train Yiga to use them! We must be ready for whatever the Magnificent One needs!"},{"seq":232,"id":"vm_kohga_047","no":"No.047","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-2127,"y":4523,"z":-454,"gx":4523,"gy":2127,"gz":-454,"title_zh":"小迦马牧场","title_en":"Little Frox Farm","place_zh":"马秋兹采矿坑","place_en":"Rist Mine","transcript_zh":"地底的怪物们太强了！如果能拉拢为伙伴一定相当可靠……！可是……它们完全驯服不了！还反过来攻击我！于是我就有了一个天才的想法！那就是“怪物培育计划”！幼患都会亲近自已的父母……我冒死捉来的小青蛙们，你们快快长大，成为魔王大人的……还有我的忠实的仆人吧！快吃快吃……啊，喂，不许咬我。都说多少次了，我不是饲料……别、别咬啦！","transcript_en":"All of the monsters down here are so strong! Stronger than a hundred men! But...none of them listen to me! The moment I find one, I get attacked. I hate getting attacked! Annnd that's why I've launched the \"Monster Training Program.\" Just as every child bonds with their parent, every monster I raise will bond with me! And they will serve the Demon King! Bwahaha—heeey! I'm not food! No I'm nooot. Stop biting meee."},{"seq":233,"id":"vm_kohga_048","no":"No.048","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":32,"y":3339,"z":-709,"gx":3339,"gy":-32,"gz":-709,"title_zh":"瘴气的真面目","title_en":"Origins of the Gloom","place_zh":"拉聂尔大水源地底","place_en":"Lanayru Great Spring Depths","transcript_zh":"遍布地底的红色东西似乎叫做瘴气。要是能早点知道是那位无上大人所散发出来的，我就能找到他了！！可现在扩散得这么广，已经不能当作线索了……之前是我无知，说瘴气有危险，是麻烦……应该没被别人听见吧……","transcript_en":"So there's a name for that red stuff I keep finding all over the Depths: gloom! I wish I'd known it was flowing from the Magnificent One—I would have just followed it to him! I can't now, though—the blasted stuff is all over the place and impossible to back track. Stupid no good... Errr... I mean... I like the Magnificent One's gloom! A lot! So much! the acoustics down here just made it SOUND like I was complaining. But I wasn't. Gloom gloom gloom!"},{"seq":234,"id":"vm_kohga_049","no":"No.049","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":1430,"y":3889,"z":-872,"gx":3889,"gy":-1430,"gz":-872,"title_zh":"背着波克布林的巨人","title_en":"The Giant and the Bokoblin","place_zh":"拉聂尔山地底","place_en":"Mount Lanayru Depths","transcript_zh":"我还以为是巨大的波克布林，下意识就准备迎战了，原来只是个石像嗯？嗯一仔细一看，那不是巨人的背吗……？他为什么会背着波克布林？是想借怪物之威吗？说起来地上也有制作怪物的面罩，企图混入怪物之中的家伙来着","transcript_en":"At first, I thought this was a giant Bokoblin—and I absolutely didn't even flinch at the sight—but it seems to just be a Statue... Hm? Hang on, is this the back? Why would there be a big Bokoblin face there? Could it be some kind of disguise? Hrm. Reminds me of that guy on the surface who makes monster masks."},{"seq":235,"id":"vm_kohga_050","no":"No.050","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":2235,"y":3545,"z":-587,"gx":3545,"gy":-2235,"gz":-587,"title_zh":"魔王的气息","title_en":"Signs of the Demon King","place_zh":"哈特诺废矿","place_en":"Abandoned Hateno Mine","transcript_zh":"瘴气是那位无上大人带来的珍贵之物……决不允许随意践踏……话虽如此，如今想要避开它也很不容易。地上那些家伙到底是怎么做的……？什么？你说地底的瘴气比地上更浓郁……？！这么重要的事情为什么不早说！那么……也就是说……那位无上大人……就在这里的某处……？！","transcript_en":"I understand that the gloom is a blessing given to us by the Magnificent One...and that stepping on it is basically an insult to him. BUT... It's really gotten all over the place. I don't know how people on the surface avoid it, even if it is less thick up there. Wait. Could that mean... The Magnificent One must be in the Depths with us!"},{"seq":236,"id":"vm_kohga_051","no":"No.051","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3383,"y":2895,"z":-452,"gx":2895,"gy":-3383,"gz":-452,"title_zh":"向阳草","title_en":"Sundelions","place_zh":"沃托里废矿","place_en":"Abandoned Lurelin Mine","transcript_zh":"从地底瘴气浓度判断，那位大人应该就在这里了……但即便是我们依盖队，也很难在不接触瘴气的情况下展开探索……话说前阵子卧底提到向阳草对瘴气有什么作用来着……让他再详细调查一下吧","transcript_en":"I'm willing to bet all my bananas that the Magnificent One is down here. The gloom is so thick...like a red oozy soup. But it's too thick for even the Yiga Clan to avoid it while searching. Wasn't there something one of my spies said about sundelions and the gloom? I'll need to look into that..."},{"seq":237,"id":"vm_kohga_052","no":"No.052","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3532,"y":2591,"z":-627,"gx":2591,"gy":-3532,"gz":-627,"title_zh":"可盖大人的心愿","title_en":"Master Kohga's Wish","place_zh":"古代地下展望台","place_en":"Ancient Observation Deck","transcript_zh":"根据笔记记载，这里好像是祈祷结缘的地方。我的心愿只有一个！让我渴见魔王大人！让我渴见魔王大人！让我渴见魔王大人！让我渴见魔王大人！","transcript_en":"The notebook says this is where people wished for matchmaking. Or something... Well, in that case, I wish to meet the Demon King! Hm... Maybe there's a trick to it? I wish to meet the Demon King! I wish to meet the Demon King! I WISH TO MEET THE DEMON KING!"},{"seq":238,"id":"vm_kohga_053","no":"No.053","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":3672,"y":362,"z":-498,"gx":362,"gy":-3672,"gz":-498,"title_zh":"依盖队据点","title_en":"Yiga Clan HQ","place_zh":"费罗尼草原地底","place_en":"Faron Grasslands Depths","transcript_zh":"地底的水源处没有怪物，也没有瘴气，是建立据点的绝佳场所。获得了合适的选址，队员们貌似也已经习惯了左纳乌装置的用法，并开始陆续创造新的设计图了。我也得抓紧完成自已的超极恶爆炎可盖尔……","transcript_en":"Monsters and gloom don't seem to like the water in the Depths, making lakes the perfect place for bases! We've already got a perfect site up and running, and the Yiga are making progress using Zonai devices. They're turning out one schematic after another! Hahaha... But also I should really get to work on...Mecha Kohga 5000 - Deluxe!"},{"seq":239,"id":"vm_kohga_054","no":"No.054","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":374,"y":-336,"z":-478,"gx":-336,"gy":-374,"gz":-478,"title_zh":"坏消息","title_en":"Unwelcome News","place_zh":"中央海拉鲁地底","place_en":"Central Hyrule Depths","transcript_zh":"我之前听说……林克那家伙下落不明，没想到还活着……但那个臭跟班绝不可能一个人回来。所以塞尔达应该已经不在这个世上了……不对那一族的人命可硬了……没亲眼看到她咽气，我还不能放心……","transcript_en":"Grrr... That cursed Link is back! I knew rumors of him vanishing were too good to be true! And where you find Link, you'll find someone pulling his strings! It can't be Zelda though. She's long gone from this world... Or is she? The royal family can be tricky... Hmmm. OK. Assume nothing, and only rest when I'm SURE the job is done!"},{"seq":240,"id":"vm_kohga_055","no":"No.055","narrator":"kohga","layer":19,"x":-963,"y":-244,"z":-1015,"gx":-244,"gy":963,"gz":-1015,"title_zh":"寻求神代的力量……","title_en":"Unlocking an Ancient Power","place_zh":"瘴气根源","place_en":"Gloom's Origin","transcript_zh":"魔王大人到底在哪里……我感觉已经距离他很近了……嗯？卧底你来啦，什么事那么着急……什什什……什么~你弄清绿色认证纹章的秘密了？就在中央大废矿啊！好！我这就过去","transcript_en":"Where could the Magnificent One be? We've searched high and low with nothing to— Hmm? Hey, you! Why are you in such a hurry? Slow down, there's no need to— What? The green crest? You've figured out how to make it work? Then we have to hurry to the Great Abandoned Central Mine! Hurry! GO FASTER!"}];
